window.CLF_EXAMS=window.CLF_EXAMS||[];
window.CLF_EXAMS.push({"id":9,"qs":[{"id":"E2B-45","d":2,"ts":"2.3.4","t":"DynamoDB TTL","q":"A web application stores user session records in an Amazon DynamoDB table. Each session should be removed 24 hours after it is created. The company wants the removal to be automatic, without consuming write capacity and without running any scheduled jobs. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Run a scheduled AWS Lambda function every hour that scans the table and deletes expired sessions.","Use a Global Secondary Index on the creation time and delete items through the index.","Enable DynamoDB Time to Live (TTL) on an attribute that stores the expiration time as a Unix epoch timestamp in seconds, set to creation time plus 24 hours.","Export the table to Amazon S3 daily and re-create the table without the old sessions."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci: 'removed 24 hours after it is created', 'automatic', 'without consuming write capacity' dan 'without running any scheduled jobs'. DynamoDB TTL menghapus item secara otomatis setelah waktu yang tersimpan di atribut TTL terlewati; atribut harus bertipe Number dengan Unix epoch time dalam detik. Penghapusan TTL tidak memakai write capacity dan tidak butuh job. Lambda yang melakukan scan dan delete memakai read dan write capacity serta menambah kode. GSI tidak menghapus apa pun. Export dan re-create tabel sangat mengganggu. Ingat: 'expire items automatically, no WCU' → DynamoDB TTL (atribut epoch detik).","r":["Salah — Scan dan delete menghabiskan RCU/WCU dan adalah job terjadwal yang ingin dihindari.","Salah — Index tidak menghapus item; penghapusan tetap memakan write capacity.","Benar — TTL menghapus item kedaluwarsa otomatis tanpa memakai WCU atau job.","Salah — Re-create tabel setiap hari mengganggu layanan dan sangat boros operasional."],"k":"Tips ujian: DynamoDB 'auto-delete old items' → TTL (Number, epoch seconds), tanpa biaya WCU."},{"id":"E2C-49","d":2,"ts":"2.4.1","t":"Lake Formation column-level security in schema design","q":"A company's curated customer table in an AWS Lake Formation data lake contains 40 columns, 6 of which hold PII such as national ID and phone number. Marketing analysts must query all non-PII columns, and only the compliance team may see PII. A data engineer proposes splitting the table into two physical tables and maintaining two ETL outputs. Which design meets the requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Keep a single table and grant marketing analysts column-level permissions (or a data filter) in Lake Formation that exclude the PII columns, while granting the compliance team full table access.","Split the table into a PII table and a non-PII table and maintain two ETL outputs as proposed.","Create a copy of the table in a separate S3 bucket for marketing with PII columns removed.","Encrypt the PII columns with a different KMS key and give the marketing team no access to the key."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah pembatasan akses pada sebagian kolom dengan 'LEAST operational overhead'. AWS Lake Formation mendukung izin pada level kolom (include/exclude columns) serta data filter untuk level baris dan sel, sehingga satu tabel dapat melayani beberapa kelompok pengguna dengan tampilan berbeda tanpa menduplikasi data. Memecah tabel menjadi dua dan memelihara dua output ETL menambah kompleksitas pipeline dan risiko inkonsistensi. Menyalin data ke bucket terpisah menciptakan duplikasi dan biaya sinkronisasi. Enkripsi kolom dengan key berbeda membutuhkan logika enkripsi di level aplikasi dan menyulitkan query, padahal Lake Formation sudah menyediakan kontrol akses kolom. Aturan umum: desain schema di Lake Formation tidak perlu memecah tabel untuk keamanan kolom; pakai column-level permissions/data filters.","r":["Benar — Izin kolom Lake Formation menyembunyikan PII dari marketing tanpa menduplikasi tabel atau pipeline.","Salah — Dua tabel dan dua output ETL menambah overhead dan risiko data tidak konsisten.","Salah — Salinan data di bucket lain menambah duplikasi, biaya, dan sinkronisasi.","Salah — Enkripsi per kolom dengan key terpisah kompleks dan menyulitkan query; kontrol akses kolom lebih sederhana."],"k":"Tips ujian: batasi kolom PII di data lake → Lake Formation column-level permissions / data filters, bukan memecah tabel."},{"id":"E2B-22","d":2,"ts":"2.2.5","t":"Glue connections with Secrets Manager","q":"A data engineer is creating an AWS Glue connection to an Amazon RDS for SQL Server database that will be used by crawlers and ETL jobs. The security team requires that the database password is never stored in plain text in Glue and is rotated automatically every 30 days without updating the Glue connection. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Store the user name and password in the Glue connection properties and update the connection with an AWS Lambda function every 30 days.","Pass the password to each job as a job parameter that is encrypted with an AWS KMS key.","Store the credentials in AWS Secrets Manager with automatic rotation enabled, and configure the Glue connection to reference the secret.","Store the password in an AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store String parameter and read it in every ETL script."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci: 'never stored in plain text in Glue' dan 'rotated automatically ... without updating the Glue connection'. Glue connection bisa mereferensikan secret di AWS Secrets Manager alih-alih menyimpan username/password langsung. Secrets Manager mendukung rotasi otomatis untuk kredensial RDS, dan karena Glue mengambil nilai secret saat runtime, connection tidak perlu diubah setiap kali password berganti. Menyimpan password di properti connection lalu memperbaruinya dengan Lambda berarti password tetap tersimpan di Glue dan butuh kode kustom. Job parameter dan Parameter Store String tidak memberi rotasi otomatis, dan String bukan tipe terenkripsi. Ingat: kredensial Glue connection + rotasi → Secrets Manager.","r":["Salah — Password tetap tersimpan di Glue, dan rotasi butuh Lambda kustom yang harus dipelihara.","Salah — Job parameter tidak memberi rotasi otomatis, dan crawler tidak memakai parameter ini.","Benar — Glue connection yang mereferensikan secret Secrets Manager mendukung rotasi otomatis tanpa mengubah connection.","Salah — Parameter String tidak terenkripsi, tidak dirotasi otomatis, dan setiap script harus diubah."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'rotate credentials automatically' untuk Glue/RDS → AWS Secrets Manager."},{"id":"E3B-33","d":3,"ts":"3.3.4","t":"Redshift query troubleshooting with system tables","q":"A data engineer investigates a slow Amazon Redshift query after a large nightly load. The STL_ALERT_EVENT_LOG table shows an alert for the query with the event 'Missing query planner statistics'. What should the engineer do FIRST?","o":["Run VACUUM DELETE ONLY on the loaded tables.","Enable concurrency scaling on the WLM queue.","Run ANALYZE on the tables that were loaded so that the query planner has current statistics.","Increase the memory percentage of the WLM queue."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kuncinya adalah pesan alert 'Missing query planner statistics' di STL_ALERT_EVENT_LOG. Tabel ini mencatat anomali eksekusi beserta solusi yang disarankan; untuk statistik yang hilang atau usang, solusinya adalah menjalankan ANALYZE agar optimizer bisa memilih rencana eksekusi (join order, distribusi) yang tepat. Distraktor terdekat adalah VACUUM, yang menangani baris terhapus dan urutan sort, bukan statistik planner. Concurrency scaling menangani lonjakan antrean, bukan rencana query yang buruk. Menambah memori queue mungkin mengurangi disk spill tetapi tidak memperbaiki statistik. Aturan: 'missing statistics' → ANALYZE; 'deleted rows / unsorted' → VACUUM.","r":["Salah — VACUUM merapikan baris terhapus, bukan memperbarui statistik planner.","Salah — Concurrency scaling menambah kapasitas untuk antrean, tidak memperbaiki rencana query.","Benar — ANALYZE memperbarui statistik sehingga planner memilih rencana eksekusi yang efisien.","Salah — Menambah memori tidak memperbaiki rencana yang dibuat dengan statistik yang hilang."],"k":"Tips ujian: STL_ALERT_EVENT_LOG 'missing statistics' → ANALYZE."},{"id":"E4B-15","d":4,"ts":"4.3.3","t":"Cross-account KMS permissions","q":"An AWS Glue job runs in Account B and must read objects from an S3 bucket in Account A. The objects are encrypted with SSE-KMS using a customer managed key in Account A. The bucket policy already allows the Glue job role to read the objects. Which TWO additional configurations are required? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Create a KMS grant in Account B on a new key that Account B owns.","Create a multi-Region replica of the key in Account B.","Add a statement to the key policy in Account A that allows the Account B Glue job role (or Account B) to use kms:Decrypt.","Add kms:Decrypt on the Account A key ARN to the IAM policy of the Glue job role in Account B.","Add the Glue job role to the S3 bucket ACL with FULL_CONTROL."],"a":[2,3],"e":"Kata kunci adalah 'customer managed key in Account A' yang dipakai oleh role di 'Account B'. Untuk akses KMS lintas akun, dibutuhkan dua izin yang saling melengkapi: key policy di akun pemilik kunci harus mengizinkan Account B (atau role spesifiknya) memakai kms:Decrypt, dan IAM policy role di Account B harus secara eksplisit mengizinkan kms:Decrypt pada ARN kunci tersebut. Tanpa salah satunya, permintaan dekripsi ditolak walaupun bucket policy sudah benar. Distraktor terdekat adalah multi-Region replica: replica key berada di akun yang sama dengan primary key di Region lain, bukan di akun lain. Grant pada kunci baru milik Account B tidak relevan karena objek dienkripsi dengan kunci Account A. ACL hanya mengatur izin S3 dan tidak menyentuh izin KMS. Aturan umum: cross-account KMS = key policy (pemilik) + IAM policy (pengguna).","r":["Salah — Objek dienkripsi dengan kunci Account A; kunci baru milik Account B tidak dapat mendekripsinya.","Salah — Multi-Region key mereplikasi kunci antar Region dalam akun yang sama, bukan ke akun lain.","Benar — Key policy di akun pemilik harus mengizinkan principal Account B untuk kms:Decrypt.","Benar — IAM policy di Account B harus mengizinkan kms:Decrypt pada ARN kunci Account A.","Salah — ACL S3 tidak memberikan izin KMS yang diperlukan untuk dekripsi."],"k":"Tips ujian: cross-account KMS selalu dua sisi — key policy di akun pemilik + IAM policy di akun pemanggil."},{"id":"E2C-22","d":2,"ts":"2.4.3","t":"DMS Schema Conversion assessment report","q":"Before committing to a migration from Microsoft SQL Server to Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL, a company's leadership wants an estimate of how much of the database schema and code can be converted automatically and which objects will require manual effort. The company does not want to provision any target database yet. Which approach meets these requirements with the LEAST effort?","o":["Create an AWS DMS Schema Conversion migration project with the SQL Server data provider and a virtual target, and generate a database migration assessment report.","Run a full AWS DMS replication task to a test Aurora cluster and count the errors in the task log.","Use AWS Glue DataBrew to profile the SQL Server tables.","Ask developers to manually review every stored procedure and estimate the conversion effort in a spreadsheet."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah 'estimate how much ... can be converted automatically', 'which objects will require manual effort', dan 'not want to provision any target database yet'. DMS Schema Conversion membaca metadata sumber dan menghasilkan assessment report yang merangkum objek yang dapat dikonversi otomatis dan action item yang membutuhkan kerja manual, sehingga cocok untuk estimasi usaha. DMS Schema Conversion juga mendukung virtual target, jadi target database belum perlu dibuat. Menjalankan replication task penuh memerlukan target dan hanya memindahkan data, bukan menilai konversi kode. DataBrew memprofilkan isi data, bukan kompatibilitas schema dan kode. Review manual memakan waktu lama dan tidak konsisten. Aturan umum: estimasi kompleksitas migrasi heterogen → assessment report dari DMS Schema Conversion.","r":["Benar — Assessment report DMS Schema Conversion menunjukkan apa yang otomatis dikonversi dan apa yang manual, dan virtual target menghindari provisioning.","Salah — Replication task membutuhkan target nyata dan tidak menilai konversi stored procedure atau kode.","Salah — DataBrew memprofilkan kualitas data, bukan kompatibilitas schema dan kode.","Salah — Review manual lambat, mahal, dan tidak konsisten dibanding report otomatis."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'estimate conversion effort' sebelum migrasi heterogen → DMS Schema Conversion assessment report."},{"id":"E1A-56","d":1,"ts":"1.1.9","t":"RDS Proxy for Lambda","q":"An AWS Lambda function is triggered by a high-volume event stream and writes each record to an Amazon RDS for MySQL database. During peaks, thousands of concurrent invocations open new connections, and the database returns 'Too many connections' errors and high CPU usage. Which solution will MOST effectively resolve the issue with minimal code changes?","o":["Increase the max_connections parameter to the highest possible value.","Move the Lambda function out of the VPC.","Place Amazon RDS Proxy between the Lambda function and the database, and connect the function to the proxy endpoint.","Increase the Lambda function's memory."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci: 'thousands of concurrent invocations open new connections' dan error 'Too many connections' dengan 'minimal code changes'. Amazon RDS Proxy mengelola connection pool di depan RDS/Aurora: ribuan invocation Lambda berbagi sejumlah kecil koneksi database, sehingga database tidak kewalahan; aplikasi cukup mengganti endpoint. Distraktor terdekat adalah menaikkan max_connections: setiap koneksi memakan memori, sehingga beban CPU/memori database justru makin tinggi dan masalah hanya tertunda. Mengeluarkan Lambda dari VPC membuatnya tidak bisa menjangkau database privat, dan memory Lambda tidak mengurangi jumlah koneksi. Aturan umum: Lambda + RDS/Aurora dengan connection storm = RDS Proxy (alternatif: batasi concurrency atau buffer dengan SQS).","r":["Salah — Lebih banyak koneksi menambah beban memori/CPU database dan hanya menunda masalah.","Salah — Database di subnet privat tidak bisa dijangkau dari Lambda di luar VPC.","Benar — RDS Proxy melakukan connection pooling sehingga ribuan invocation berbagi sedikit koneksi.","Salah — Memory Lambda tidak memengaruhi jumlah koneksi yang dibuka ke database."],"k":"Lambda → RDS 'too many connections' → RDS Proxy (connection pooling)."},{"id":"E1C-23","d":1,"ts":"1.3.2","t":"Long-running tasks in serverless workflows","q":"A transformation step in a Step Functions workflow runs a containerized Python program that depends on custom native libraries. The step takes 40 to 90 minutes, and it currently runs as an AWS Lambda function that times out. The team wants to keep the workflow serverless and avoid managing servers. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Increase the Lambda function timeout to 2 hours.","Split the program into many Lambda functions that each run for 15 minutes and pass state through the function memory.","Run the container on Amazon ECS with AWS Fargate by using the Step Functions ecs:runTask.sync integration.","Run the program on a self-managed Amazon EC2 instance that the workflow starts and stops."],"a":[2],"e":"Batasannya: proses '40 to 90 minutes', berbentuk container dengan library native, dan 'avoid managing servers'. Lambda memiliki batas keras 15 menit sehingga tidak bisa dinaikkan menjadi 2 jam. Amazon ECS dengan Fargate menjalankan container tanpa server yang perlu dikelola dan tanpa batas waktu 15 menit, dan integrasi '.sync' Step Functions menunggu task selesai lalu meneruskan status sukses/gagal. Distractor terdekat adalah memecah ke banyak Lambda: memori fungsi tidak bertahan antar invocation, jadi state harus disimpan di luar dan kompleksitas melonjak. EC2 self-managed melanggar syarat tanpa pengelolaan server. Aturan umum: pekerjaan lebih dari 15 menit dalam workflow serverless → ECS Fargate (atau AWS Batch/Glue) dengan integrasi .sync.","r":["Salah — Timeout Lambda maksimum 15 menit dan tidak bisa dinaikkan.","Salah — Memori Lambda tidak persisten antar invocation; pemecahan seperti ini rapuh dan kompleks.","Benar — Fargate menjalankan container lama tanpa server, dan runTask.sync membuat workflow menunggu hasilnya.","Salah — EC2 self-managed menambah overhead pengelolaan server."],"k":"Tips ujian: proses > 15 menit + container + serverless → ECS Fargate dengan Step Functions .sync."},{"id":"E1A-10","d":1,"ts":"1.1.2","t":"DynamoDB export to S3","q":"An analytics team needs a full copy of a 3 TB Amazon DynamoDB table in Amazon S3 every night so that it can be queried with Amazon Athena. The export must not consume the table's read capacity or affect production traffic. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Enable point-in-time recovery on the table and use an Amazon EventBridge Scheduler schedule to start a DynamoDB export to Amazon S3 every night.","Run an AWS Lambda function that performs a parallel Scan of the table and writes JSON files to Amazon S3.","Run an AWS Glue ETL job that scans the DynamoDB table and writes the results to Amazon S3.","Create an Amazon EMR cluster with Apache Hive to read the DynamoDB table and write to Amazon S3."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: 'must not consume the table's read capacity' dan 'LEAST operational overhead'. Fitur DynamoDB export to S3 bekerja dari data point-in-time recovery (PITR), sehingga tidak memakai RCU dan tidak mengganggu trafik produksi; outputnya (DynamoDB JSON atau Ion) bisa langsung di-query dengan Athena. Prasyaratnya PITR harus diaktifkan; fitur export tidak punya jadwal bawaan, jadi jadwal malam cukup dibuat dengan EventBridge Scheduler yang memanggil API ExportTableToPointInTime. Distraktor terdekat adalah Glue ETL job: mudah, tetapi Scan tabel memakai read capacity (bisa dibatasi dengan persentase throughput, namun tetap memakai kapasitas). Lambda parallel Scan juga memakai RCU dan sulit untuk tabel 3 TB karena batas waktu 15 menit. EMR menambah overhead cluster. Aturan umum: salinan DynamoDB ke S3 tanpa memakai RCU = DynamoDB export to S3 (butuh PITR).","r":["Benar — Export to S3 berbasis PITR tidak memakai read capacity dan fully managed; Scheduler cukup memanggil API ExportTableToPointInTime setiap malam.","Salah — Scan memakai RCU, dan tabel 3 TB sulit diselesaikan dalam batas waktu Lambda.","Salah — Glue job yang melakukan scan langsung ke tabel DynamoDB memakai read capacity tabel.","Salah — EMR + Hive juga memakai read capacity dan menambah pengelolaan cluster."],"k":"DynamoDB → S3 tanpa memakai RCU → DynamoDB export to S3 (aktifkan PITR)."},{"id":"E3B-47","d":3,"ts":"3.4.2","t":"DataBrew data quality rulesets","q":"A data team already uses AWS Glue DataBrew projects to prepare datasets in Amazon S3. Data stewards, who do not write code, now want to define checks such as 'duplicate rows must be 0' and 'missing values in customer_id must be less than 1%' and have them validated automatically on every new daily file. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Create a DataBrew data quality ruleset for the dataset and attach it to a scheduled DataBrew profile job.","Add the checks as steps in a DataBrew recipe job.","Write Deequ checks in Scala and run them on Amazon EMR.","Create an AWS Glue crawler with a schema change policy."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kuncinya: tim 'already uses DataBrew', data steward 'do not write code', dan aturan harus 'validated automatically on every new daily file'. DataBrew data quality rulesets memungkinkan definisi aturan secara visual (misalnya jumlah duplicate rows, persentase missing values, nilai kolom) dengan threshold. Ruleset dievaluasi oleh DataBrew profile job, dan profile job dapat dijadwalkan sehingga setiap file baru divalidasi dan menghasilkan laporan validasi. Distraktor terdekat adalah recipe job: recipe berfungsi untuk transformasi data, bukan mengevaluasi ruleset. Deequ di EMR butuh kode Scala. Crawler hanya memantau skema. Aturan: aturan kualitas data di DataBrew → ruleset + profile job.","r":["Benar — Ruleset DataBrew didefinisikan secara visual dan dievaluasi oleh profile job terjadwal.","Salah — Recipe job menjalankan transformasi, tidak mengevaluasi ruleset kualitas data.","Salah — Butuh kode Scala dan pengelolaan cluster, bertentangan dengan pengguna non-coder.","Salah — Crawler mendeteksi perubahan skema, bukan aturan nilai data."],"k":"Tips ujian: DataBrew data quality rules → ruleset dievaluasi oleh profile job (bukan recipe job)."},{"id":"E3A-15","d":3,"ts":"3.1.4","t":"Amazon EMR cost-efficient processing","q":"A company runs Apache Spark batch jobs on Amazon EMR on EC2 once every night. The cluster currently runs 24 hours a day even though the jobs take about 3 hours. The input and output data are stored in Amazon S3. The jobs can be retried if some capacity is lost. Which TWO actions will MOST reduce cost? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Launch a transient cluster each night that runs the jobs as EMR steps and automatically terminates after the last step completes.","Use Spot Instances for the primary node to get the largest discount.","Use instance fleets with Spot Instances for the task nodes and On-Demand Instances for the primary and core nodes.","Store intermediate and final results in HDFS instead of Amazon S3.","Purchase a Savings Plan for the cluster's 24-hour usage and keep the cluster running."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Ada dua sumber pemborosan: cluster 'runs 24 hours a day' padahal kerja hanya 3 jam, dan semua kapasitas memakai harga penuh. Cluster transient yang menjalankan job sebagai EMR steps lalu auto-terminate menghilangkan 21 jam biaya idle; ini aman karena data disimpan di S3 (EMRFS), bukan di cluster. Spot Instances untuk task node memberi diskon besar, dan task node tidak menyimpan data HDFS sehingga kehilangan Spot hanya memperlambat job. Primary node di Spot berisiko: jika diambil kembali, seluruh cluster mati. Menyimpan hasil di HDFS membuat data hilang saat cluster transient dimatikan. Savings Plan untuk cluster yang terus menyala tetap membayar 21 jam idle setiap hari. Aturan umum EMR hemat: transient cluster + data di S3 + Spot untuk task node.","r":["Benar — Cluster transient dengan auto-terminate menghilangkan biaya idle 21 jam per hari.","Salah — Primary node di Spot dapat mematikan seluruh cluster saat instance diambil kembali.","Benar — Spot untuk task node memberi diskon besar dengan risiko rendah karena task node tidak menyimpan HDFS.","Salah — HDFS hilang saat cluster transient dimatikan; S3 adalah penyimpanan persisten yang tepat.","Salah — Savings Plan tetap membayar kapasitas idle; mematikan cluster jauh lebih hemat."],"k":"Tips ujian: EMR batch berkala → transient cluster + EMR steps + auto-terminate; Spot untuk task node, bukan primary."},{"id":"E4B-10","d":4,"ts":"4.3.2","t":"Redshift encryption at rest","q":"A company has an existing unencrypted Amazon Redshift provisioned cluster with RA3 nodes. A new policy requires that the cluster data be encrypted at rest with a customer managed AWS KMS key that the security team can audit and control. The company wants to minimize the effort and avoid rebuilding data pipelines. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Unload all tables to Amazon S3, create a new encrypted cluster with the customer managed key, and reload the data with COPY commands.","Modify the cluster to enable encryption and select the customer managed KMS key, allowing Amazon Redshift to migrate the data to an encrypted cluster automatically.","Set the require_ssl parameter to true in the cluster parameter group.","Enable SSE-KMS default encryption on the S3 bucket used for automated snapshots."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: cluster yang sudah ada harus dienkripsi 'at rest with a customer managed AWS KMS key' dengan 'minimize the effort and avoid rebuilding data pipelines'. Amazon Redshift mendukung perubahan enkripsi pada cluster yang ada melalui modify cluster: Anda memilih KMS key, lalu Redshift memigrasikan data ke cluster terenkripsi secara otomatis (selama migrasi cluster berstatus resizing dan hanya bisa dibaca), sehingga pipeline tidak perlu dibangun ulang. Jika cross-Region snapshot copy aktif, fitur itu harus dinonaktifkan dulu sebelum mengubah enkripsi. Distraktor terdekat adalah UNLOAD lalu COPY ke cluster baru: hasil akhirnya terenkripsi, tetapi upayanya jauh lebih besar dan endpoint berubah. require_ssl hanya memaksa enkripsi in transit, bukan at rest. Snapshot Redshift dikelola oleh layanan dan tidak bisa dienkripsi dengan mengubah default encryption bucket S3 milik Anda. Aturan umum: enkripsi at rest Redshift yang sudah ada → modify cluster encryption dengan KMS key.","r":["Salah — Berhasil secara teknis, tetapi membutuhkan upaya migrasi besar dan perubahan endpoint/pipeline.","Benar — Modify cluster encryption memakai customer managed key dan Redshift menangani migrasi data secara otomatis.","Salah — require_ssl mengatur enkripsi in transit, bukan enkripsi data at rest.","Salah — Snapshot Redshift dikelola layanan; default encryption bucket tidak mengenkripsi data cluster."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'encrypt existing Redshift cluster with KMS' → modify cluster encryption (bukan unload/reload)."},{"id":"E2C-10","d":2,"ts":"2.4.1","t":"DynamoDB sparse indexes","q":"An Amazon DynamoDB table stores 200 million support tickets. Fewer than 1% of tickets are in the ESCALATED state at any time, and a dashboard must list all escalated tickets every minute. The data engineer wants to minimize read and storage cost for this access pattern. Which design should be used?","o":["Scan the whole table every minute with a filter expression on status = 'ESCALATED'.","Create a GSI on the status attribute for all items and query the partition for 'ESCALATED'.","Write an escalated_at attribute only on escalated tickets, remove it when the ticket is de-escalated, and create a sparse GSI with escalated_at as a key attribute.","Export the table to Amazon S3 every minute and query the export with Amazon Athena."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah 'fewer than 1% of tickets' dan 'minimize read and storage cost'. Sparse index di DynamoDB memanfaatkan sifat GSI yang hanya berisi item yang memiliki atribut key index; jika atribut escalated_at hanya ada pada tiket yang escalated, GSI hanya berisi kurang dari 1% item. Query terhadap GSI kecil ini murah, dan storage serta biaya replikasi tulisan ke index juga minimal. GSI pada status untuk semua item menyimpan 200 juta entri dan menciptakan partisi panas dengan sedikit nilai berbeda. Scan setiap menit membaca seluruh tabel sehingga sangat mahal. Export ke S3 setiap menit tidak praktis dan berlatensi tinggi. Aturan umum: subset kecil item yang sering di-query → sparse GSI dengan atribut yang hanya ditulis pada item tersebut.","r":["Salah — Scan setiap menit membaca 200 juta item dan biaya dihitung dari data yang dibaca, bukan hasil filter.","Salah — GSI pada status berisi semua item, sehingga storage index besar dan nilai berkardinalitas rendah menimbulkan hot partition.","Benar — Sparse GSI hanya berisi item yang punya escalated_at sehingga query dan storage index sangat kecil.","Salah — Export setiap menit lambat, mahal, dan berlebihan untuk kebutuhan dashboard ini."],"k":"Tips ujian: query subset kecil item di DynamoDB → sparse index (atribut hanya ada pada item target)."},{"id":"E1B-45","d":1,"ts":"1.2.6","t":"Glue Relationalize for nested data","q":"A data engineer receives deeply nested JSON documents that contain arrays of line items and nested address objects. The data must be loaded into normalized tables in Amazon Redshift. The engineer wants to flatten the nested structures and split arrays into separate tables with the LEAST custom code. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Load the raw JSON into a single VARCHAR column in Redshift and parse it with string functions in every query.","Write a recursive Python function in AWS Lambda that walks each document and generates INSERT statements.","Use the AWS Glue Relationalize transform on a DynamicFrame to flatten nested fields and pivot arrays into separate tables, and then write them to Redshift.","Convert the JSON to CSV with Amazon Data Firehose and then load it with COPY."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kuncinya adalah JSON 'deeply nested' dengan 'arrays of line items', target 'normalized tables in Amazon Redshift', dan 'LEAST custom code'. Transform Relationalize pada Glue DynamicFrame secara otomatis meratakan struktur bersarang menjadi kolom dan memecah array menjadi tabel terpisah dengan kunci penghubung, sehingga hasilnya langsung cocok untuk skema relasional. Menyimpan JSON mentah di VARCHAR dan mem-parsing di setiap query membuat query lambat dan tidak menghasilkan tabel ternormalisasi. Lambda rekursif yang membuat INSERT berarti banyak kode kustom dan loading baris per baris yang lambat. Firehose tidak memiliki konversi JSON ke CSV bawaan untuk struktur bersarang. Aturan umum: nested JSON → tabel relasional di Glue → Relationalize.","r":["Salah — Parsing berulang di setiap query lambat dan tidak menghasilkan tabel ternormalisasi.","Salah — Membutuhkan banyak kode kustom dan INSERT baris per baris lambat di Redshift.","Benar — Relationalize meratakan struktur bersarang dan memecah array menjadi tabel terpisah dengan kode minimal.","Salah — Firehose tidak meratakan JSON bersarang menjadi beberapa tabel relasional."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'flatten nested JSON into relational tables' → Glue Relationalize transform."},{"id":"E2B-53","d":2,"ts":"2.3.5","t":"Deleting data from Redshift and snapshots","q":"A legal request requires that all rows for a specific customer be removed from an Amazon Redshift provisioned cluster, including from any recovery points that the company controls, within 35 days. Automated snapshots are retained for 7 days, and the team also keeps manual snapshots for 1 year. Which TWO actions will meet these requirements? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Run DELETE for the customer's rows, and then run VACUUM DELETE ONLY on the affected tables to reclaim the space of the deleted rows.","Run UNLOAD for the customer's rows to Amazon S3 and then delete the unloaded files.","Delete, or recreate after the deletion, the manual snapshots that contain the customer's rows, because manual snapshots are not removed automatically.","Run ANALYZE on the affected tables to remove the deleted rows.","Increase the automated snapshot retention period to 35 days."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Kata kunci: 'all rows ... be removed', 'including from any recovery points' dan 'within 35 days'. Di Redshift, DELETE hanya menandai baris sebagai terhapus; VACUUM DELETE ONLY (atau automatic vacuum delete) yang benar-benar mengklaim ulang ruang dari baris tersebut. Snapshot otomatis dengan retensi 7 hari akan kedaluwarsa sendiri dalam batas 35 hari. Snapshot manual disimpan sampai dihapus atau sampai periode retensinya habis (di sini 1 tahun), sehingga snapshot yang berisi data pelanggan harus dihapus atau diganti dengan snapshot baru yang dibuat setelah penghapusan. UNLOAD menyalin data, bukan menghapusnya dari tabel. ANALYZE hanya memperbarui statistik. Memperpanjang retensi snapshot otomatis justru menyimpan data lebih lama. Ingat: penghapusan legal mencakup data aktif dan backup; Redshift DELETE + VACUUM, dan kelola snapshot manual.","r":["Benar — DELETE ditambah VACUUM DELETE ONLY menghapus baris dan mengklaim ulang ruang penyimpanannya.","Salah — UNLOAD hanya menyalin baris ke S3; baris tetap ada di Redshift.","Benar — Snapshot manual bertahan sampai dihapus atau retensinya habis, jadi harus ditangani agar data tidak tersisa.","Salah — ANALYZE memperbarui statistik optimizer dan tidak menghapus data.","Salah — Retensi lebih panjang menyimpan data pelanggan lebih lama di backup."],"k":"Tips ujian: legal delete di Redshift → DELETE + VACUUM, dan jangan lupa snapshot manual (tidak kedaluwarsa otomatis kecuali diberi retensi)."},{"id":"E1B-34","d":1,"ts":"1.2.4","t":"AWS Glue Auto Scaling","q":"An AWS Glue Spark job processes daily input that varies between 5 GB on most days and 500 GB at month end. The job is configured with a fixed 100 G.2X workers so that it can handle the month-end volume, and most daily runs leave workers idle. Which solution will reduce cost while still handling the peak volume?","o":["Reduce the job to 10 G.2X workers permanently.","Enable AWS Glue Auto Scaling and set the maximum number of workers to the value needed for the month-end volume.","Change the worker type to G.1X while keeping 100 workers.","Split the job into 100 separate jobs that each use one worker."],"a":[1],"e":"Penentunya adalah volume yang 'varies between 5 GB ... and 500 GB' dengan konfigurasi tetap 100 worker sehingga sebagian besar run membiarkan worker 'idle'. Glue Auto Scaling (Glue 3.0 ke atas) menambah dan melepas worker secara dinamis sesuai kebutuhan setiap tahap, dengan jumlah worker yang dikonfigurasi sebagai batas maksimum, sehingga run harian kecil hanya membayar worker yang dipakai dan run akhir bulan tetap bisa mencapai kapasitas penuh. Mengurangi permanen ke 10 worker memangkas biaya, tetapi run akhir bulan akan sangat lambat atau gagal. G.1X dengan 100 worker tetap over-provisioned dan memori per worker berkurang. Memecah menjadi 100 job menambah kompleksitas orkestrasi. Aturan umum: beban Glue yang bervariasi → Auto Scaling dengan batas maksimum.","r":["Salah — Hemat untuk hari biasa, tetapi tidak sanggup menangani volume akhir bulan.","Benar — Auto Scaling menyesuaikan worker dengan beban dan hanya menagih worker yang aktif.","Salah — Tetap over-provisioned di hari biasa dan mengurangi memori per worker untuk puncak.","Salah — Menambah kompleksitas orkestrasi tanpa menyelesaikan masalah kapasitas dinamis."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'Glue workload size varies / idle workers' → enable Glue Auto Scaling (max workers)."},{"id":"E1B-22","d":1,"ts":"1.2.2","t":"Redshift JDBC with IAM authentication","q":"A company runs a Java-based data processing service on Amazon ECS that must query an Amazon Redshift provisioned cluster. The security team requires that no database passwords be stored in the application, configuration files, or environment variables. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Store the database user password in an environment variable of the ECS task definition.","Use the Redshift ODBC driver with a DSN file that contains the database user and password.","Make the Redshift cluster publicly accessible and allow connections only from the ECS task public IP addresses.","Use the Amazon Redshift JDBC driver with IAM authentication so that the ECS task role obtains temporary database credentials."],"a":[3],"e":"Penentunya adalah aplikasi 'Java-based' dan larangan menyimpan password di aplikasi, file konfigurasi, maupun environment variable. Driver JDBC Redshift mendukung autentikasi IAM: aplikasi memakai kredensial IAM role task ECS untuk memperoleh kredensial database sementara (misalnya melalui GetClusterCredentials), sehingga tidak ada password statis yang disimpan. Environment variable dan file DSN ODBC jelas menyimpan password, dan ODBC kurang tepat untuk aplikasi Java. Membuat cluster publik tidak menghilangkan kebutuhan password dan menambah risiko eksposur. Aturan umum: koneksi aplikasi ke Redshift tanpa password statis → JDBC/ODBC driver dengan IAM authentication (temporary credentials).","r":["Salah — Environment variable tetap menyimpan password, melanggar kebijakan keamanan.","Salah — DSN file menyimpan password, dan aplikasi Java lebih tepat memakai JDBC.","Salah — Akses publik tidak menghilangkan kebutuhan password dan memperluas permukaan serangan.","Benar — IAM authentication di driver JDBC menghasilkan kredensial sementara dari IAM role tanpa password tersimpan."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'connect to Redshift without storing passwords' → JDBC/ODBC driver + IAM authentication (temporary credentials)."},{"id":"E1B-67","d":1,"ts":"1.2.10","t":"Redshift ML integration with Bedrock","q":"Analysts work only in SQL in Amazon Redshift. They want to classify free-text customer complaints stored in a Redshift table into categories by using a large language model, and to store the results in a new column. The company wants to avoid exporting the data or building separate pipelines. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["UNLOAD the table to Amazon S3, process the files with an AWS Glue job that calls a model, and COPY the results back.","Export the table to a CSV file and process it with a Python script on an analyst's laptop.","Use a Redshift user-defined function written in Python that performs keyword matching.","Use Amazon Redshift ML with CREATE EXTERNAL MODEL to reference an Amazon Bedrock model, and call the generated SQL function in an UPDATE or SELECT statement."],"a":[3],"e":"Penentunya adalah analis yang bekerja 'only in SQL' di Redshift, kebutuhan klasifikasi teks dengan 'large language model', serta larangan mengekspor data atau membangun pipeline terpisah. Amazon Redshift ML terintegrasi dengan Amazon Bedrock: perintah CREATE EXTERNAL MODEL membuat objek model dan fungsi SQL yang memanggil model Bedrock, sehingga LLM dapat dipanggil langsung dari query SQL atas data di tabel. UNLOAD → Glue → COPY berfungsi, tetapi itu adalah pipeline terpisah yang memindahkan data. Ekspor ke laptop melanggar praktik keamanan dan tidak skalabel. UDF keyword matching bukan LLM dan akurasinya rendah untuk teks bebas; selain itu, Redshift tidak lagi mendukung Python UDF setelah 30 Juni 2026. Aturan umum: LLM dari SQL di Redshift → Redshift ML + Bedrock (CREATE EXTERNAL MODEL).","r":["Salah — Membangun pipeline terpisah dan memindahkan data keluar-masuk Redshift.","Salah — Mengekspor data ke laptop tidak aman dan tidak skalabel.","Salah — Keyword matching bukan LLM dan kurang akurat untuk klasifikasi teks bebas; Python UDF di Redshift juga tidak lagi didukung setelah 30 Juni 2026.","Benar — Redshift ML dengan CREATE EXTERNAL MODEL memanggil model Bedrock langsung dari SQL."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'call an LLM from SQL in Redshift' → Redshift ML CREATE EXTERNAL MODEL dengan MODEL_TYPE BEDROCK."},{"id":"E2A-49","d":2,"ts":"2.1.6","t":"RDS PostgreSQL lock management","q":"Nightly maintenance on an Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL database keeps failing because an ALTER TABLE statement times out waiting for a lock. Investigation shows that an application sometimes opens a transaction, runs a SELECT, and then leaves the connection 'idle in transaction' for hours. Which TWO actions should a data engineer take to find the blocking sessions and prevent the problem from recurring? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Query the pg_locks and pg_stat_activity views to identify the blocking process IDs, and end them with pg_terminate_backend.","Reboot the DB instance with failover every night before the maintenance window.","Set the idle_in_transaction_session_timeout parameter in the DB parameter group so idle transactions are terminated automatically.","Convert the DB instance to a Multi-AZ deployment so the standby handles the ALTER TABLE.","Increase the max_connections parameter so the ALTER TABLE can use a new connection."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Kata kunci adalah sesi yang 'idle in transaction' memegang lock berjam-jam dan kebutuhan untuk 'find the blocking sessions' serta 'prevent the problem from recurring'. Di PostgreSQL, view pg_locks dan pg_stat_activity menunjukkan lock yang dipegang/ditunggu, status sesi, dan PID, lalu pg_terminate_backend(pid) menghentikan sesi penghalang. Untuk pencegahan, parameter idle_in_transaction_session_timeout di DB parameter group otomatis memutus sesi yang terlalu lama idle di dalam transaksi, sehingga lock dilepas. Distraktor terdekat adalah reboot setiap malam: melepas lock, tetapi menimbulkan downtime dan tidak memperbaiki akar masalah. Standby Multi-AZ tidak menjalankan DDL terpisah, dan menambah max_connections tidak mengubah konflik lock. Aturan umum: lock di RDS PostgreSQL → pg_locks/pg_stat_activity + pg_terminate_backend; cegah dengan timeout sesi idle.","r":["Benar — pg_locks dan pg_stat_activity mengidentifikasi PID penghalang, dan pg_terminate_backend melepaskan lock-nya.","Salah — Reboot setiap malam menyebabkan downtime dan tidak menghilangkan perilaku aplikasi yang menahan transaksi.","Benar — idle_in_transaction_session_timeout otomatis mengakhiri sesi idle dalam transaksi sehingga lock tidak tertahan lama.","Salah — Standby Multi-AZ hanya untuk failover dan tidak dapat menjalankan DDL secara terpisah.","Salah — Koneksi baru tetap harus menunggu lock yang sama; jumlah koneksi bukan masalahnya."],"k":"RDS PostgreSQL blocking → pg_locks/pg_stat_activity + pg_terminate_backend; prevent with idle_in_transaction_session_timeout."},{"id":"E1B-56","d":1,"ts":"1.2.8","t":"Amazon Redshift Data API","q":"A data engineer is building an AWS Lambda-based microservice that must run SQL queries against an Amazon Redshift Serverless workgroup and return results to other systems. The engineer wants to avoid packaging database drivers, managing persistent connections or connection pools, and handling credentials in code. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Use the Amazon Redshift Data API from the Lambda function to submit SQL statements asynchronously and retrieve results.","Package the Redshift JDBC driver in a Lambda layer and open a new connection on each invocation.","Use Amazon RDS Proxy in front of the Redshift workgroup to pool connections.","Unload query results to Amazon S3 every hour and have Lambda read the files."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci penentunya adalah 'avoid packaging database drivers', 'managing persistent connections', dan tidak menangani kredensial di kode. Redshift Data API adalah API HTTPS yang dapat dipanggil lewat AWS SDK untuk mengirim SQL secara asinkron ke cluster provisioned atau Redshift Serverless dan mengambil hasilnya, dengan autentikasi IAM atau Secrets Manager sehingga tidak ada driver dan koneksi persisten. Driver JDBC di Lambda layer adalah distraktor terdekat karena berfungsi, tetapi justru mengemas driver dan membuka koneksi di setiap invocation. RDS Proxy adalah fitur untuk RDS/Aurora, bukan Redshift. UNLOAD per jam tidak memberikan hasil query sesuai permintaan. Aturan umum: aplikasi serverless/web menjalankan SQL ke Redshift tanpa driver → Redshift Data API.","r":["Benar — Data API menjalankan SQL lewat HTTPS secara asinkron tanpa driver, koneksi persisten, atau kredensial di kode.","Salah — Mengemas driver dan membuka koneksi setiap invocation bertentangan dengan persyaratan.","Salah — RDS Proxy tidak mendukung Amazon Redshift.","Salah — Data per jam tidak mendukung query on-demand dari sistem lain."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'Lambda/app → Redshift SQL without drivers or connection management' → Redshift Data API."},{"id":"E1C-59","d":1,"ts":"1.4.4","t":"Structured logging and metric filters","q":"An AWS Lambda ingestion function writes free-text log lines with print statements. The operations team cannot easily search logs by batch_id, and they want an alarm when the number of rejected records in a 5-minute period exceeds 1,000, without adding new infrastructure. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Write structured JSON log entries that include batch_id and rejected_count to Amazon CloudWatch Logs, create a metric filter that extracts rejected_count into a CloudWatch metric, and create a CloudWatch alarm on that metric.","Write logs to a file in the function's /tmp directory and upload the file to Amazon S3 once a day for analysis.","Enable AWS CloudTrail data events for the function and alarm on the number of Invoke API calls.","Increase the log retention period of the log group to 10 years."],"a":[0],"e":"Kebutuhannya: log yang bisa dicari per 'batch_id' dan alarm saat 'rejected records ... exceeds 1,000' dalam 5 menit, 'without adding new infrastructure'. Structured logging dalam format JSON membuat field seperti batch_id dapat dicari dan dianalisis dengan CloudWatch Logs Insights. Metric filter CloudWatch Logs dapat mengekstrak nilai numerik rejected_count dari log JSON menjadi metrik, dan alarm CloudWatch dengan periode 5 menit dan statistik Sum memicu notifikasi. Distractor terdekat adalah CloudTrail data events: hanya mencatat panggilan API Invoke, bukan isi pemrosesan atau jumlah record yang ditolak. File di /tmp hilang saat environment didaur ulang dan analisis harian tidak real time. Retensi lebih lama tidak membuat log lebih mudah dicari. Aturan umum: logging terstruktur (JSON) + metric filter + alarm untuk monitoring pipeline.","r":["Benar — Log JSON dapat dikueri per field, dan metric filter + alarm memberi peringatan tanpa infrastruktur baru.","Salah — /tmp tidak persisten dan analisis harian tidak memberi alarm 5 menit.","Salah — CloudTrail mencatat panggilan API, bukan jumlah record yang ditolak.","Salah — Retensi tidak meningkatkan kemampuan pencarian atau memberi alarm."],"k":"Tips ujian: monitoring dari log aplikasi → structured JSON logs + CloudWatch metric filter + alarm."},{"id":"E2B-57","d":2,"ts":"2.3.6","t":"DynamoDB point-in-time recovery","q":"A DynamoDB table stores order data for a high-traffic application. A faulty deployment can corrupt items, and the operations team must be able to restore the table to its state at any second within the last few weeks before the corruption occurred. Which solution meets this requirement with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Create on-demand backups every hour with an Amazon EventBridge schedule.","Enable point-in-time recovery (PITR) on the table and restore to a new table at the required timestamp when needed.","Enable DynamoDB Streams and replay all changes from the beginning into a new table.","Export the table to Amazon S3 every night and import the export when needed."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: 'restore ... to its state at any second within the last few weeks' dan 'LEAST operational overhead'. DynamoDB point-in-time recovery memberi pemulihan kontinu dengan granularitas per detik dalam periode pemulihan hingga 35 hari, tanpa memengaruhi performa tabel dan tanpa jadwal backup. Restore selalu dilakukan ke tabel baru. Backup on-demand per jam hanya memberi titik pemulihan tiap jam dan menambah penjadwalan. Streams hanya menyimpan data selama 24 jam, jadi tidak bisa memutar ulang beberapa minggu. Export harian ke S3 memberi RPO hingga 24 jam. Ingat: 'any point in time / per second' untuk DynamoDB → PITR (hingga 35 hari).","r":["Salah — Backup per jam tidak memberi pemulihan per detik dan menambah penjadwalan.","Benar — PITR memungkinkan restore ke detik mana pun dalam periode pemulihan tanpa pengelolaan backup.","Salah — Streams hanya menyimpan perubahan 24 jam dan replay butuh kode kustom.","Salah — Export harian hanya memberi satu titik pemulihan per hari."],"k":"Tips ujian: DynamoDB 'restore to any second' → point-in-time recovery (hingga 35 hari, restore ke tabel baru)."},{"id":"E1C-34","d":1,"ts":"1.3.3","t":"Step Functions JSONata and intrinsic functions","q":"A Step Functions workflow uses four small AWS Lambda functions whose only purpose is to rename JSON fields, concatenate strings, and build the input for the next state. The team wants to reduce latency, cost, and the number of functions to maintain. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Merge the four functions into one larger Lambda function.","Replace the functions with Pass states that use JSONata expressions or Step Functions intrinsic functions to transform the state data.","Move the transformations into an Amazon EventBridge input transformer on a separate rule.","Increase the memory of each Lambda function to reduce its duration."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kuncinya: Lambda yang 'only purpose is to rename ... concatenate ... build the input', dengan tujuan mengurangi 'latency, cost, and the number of functions'. Step Functions mendukung transformasi data di dalam state machine melalui intrinsic functions (misalnya States.Format, States.JsonMerge) dan JSONata, sehingga manipulasi payload sederhana bisa dilakukan di Pass state atau field Arguments/Output tanpa Lambda. Distractor terdekat adalah menggabungkan menjadi satu Lambda: jumlah fungsi berkurang, tetapi biaya dan latensi invocation masih ada. Input transformer EventBridge hanya berlaku saat event dikirim ke target, bukan di antara state. Menambah memori tidak menghilangkan fungsi. Aturan umum: transformasi payload sederhana di Step Functions → JSONata/intrinsic functions, bukan Lambda.","r":["Salah — Masih ada fungsi yang harus dipelihara dan dibayar.","Benar — JSONata atau intrinsic functions mentransformasi data langsung di state machine tanpa Lambda.","Salah — Input transformer hanya berlaku pada target rule EventBridge, bukan antar state.","Salah — Fungsi tetap ada dan menambah biaya memori."],"k":"Tips ujian: Lambda hanya untuk reshape JSON di workflow → pakai JSONata/intrinsic functions."},{"id":"E2C-45","d":2,"ts":"2.4.6","t":"Embedding dimensions trade-off","q":"A company plans to embed 200 million text chunks with Amazon Titan Text Embeddings V2 for a Bedrock knowledge base. The vector store cost is a major concern, and the team has measured that retrieval accuracy drops only slightly with smaller vectors for its use case. Which configuration change will MOST reduce vector storage cost?","o":["Increase the chunk overlap percentage so that fewer chunks are created.","Use the 1,024-dimension output, which is the model's default.","Configure the embeddings model to output 256-dimension vectors instead of 1,024 dimensions.","Store the raw text instead of vectors in the vector store."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah 'vector store cost is a major concern' dan retrieval accuracy 'drops only slightly with smaller vectors'. Amazon Titan Text Embeddings V2 mendukung ukuran output 1.024 (default), 512, atau 256 dimensi. Ukuran storage vektor berbanding lurus dengan jumlah dimensi, sehingga 256 dimensi memakai sekitar seperempat storage dibanding 1.024 dengan sedikit penurunan akurasi. Menaikkan overlap justru menambah teks duplikat dan bisa menambah jumlah chunk. Tetap memakai 1.024 dimensi tidak mengurangi biaya. Menyimpan teks mentah tanpa vektor menghilangkan kemampuan similarity search. Aturan umum: trade-off dimensi embedding → dimensi lebih kecil = storage dan biaya lebih rendah, akurasi sedikit turun; dimensi lebih besar = representasi lebih kaya.","r":["Salah — Overlap lebih besar menambah teks duplikat dan tidak mengurangi ukuran per vektor.","Salah — 1.024 dimensi adalah ukuran terbesar sehingga biaya storage tertinggi.","Benar — 256 dimensi mengurangi storage vektor sekitar 75% dengan penurunan akurasi kecil.","Salah — Tanpa vektor, similarity search tidak bisa dilakukan."],"k":"Tips ujian: kurangi biaya vector store → turunkan dimensi embedding (Titan V2: 1024/512/256)."},{"id":"E4A-35","d":4,"ts":"4.2.2","t":"Cross-account Secrets Manager access","q":"A database secret in AWS Secrets Manager in account A is encrypted with the default AWS managed key aws/secretsmanager. An AWS Glue job in account B must read the secret. The secret's resource policy already allows the Glue job role from account B, and the role's IAM policy allows secretsmanager:GetSecretValue on the secret ARN, but the job still fails. What should a data engineer do?","o":["Add the Glue job role to the key policy of the aws/secretsmanager key in account A.","Re-encrypt the secret with a customer managed KMS key in account A whose key policy allows the account B role to use kms:Decrypt, and grant kms:Decrypt on that key in the role's IAM policy.","Replicate the secret to account B by using Secrets Manager multi-Region replication.","Copy the secret value into an AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store parameter in account B."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: dienkripsi dengan 'default AWS managed key aws/secretsmanager' dan dibaca dari 'account B'. Key policy AWS managed key tidak bisa diubah, sehingga principal dari akun lain tidak pernah bisa memakai key tersebut untuk mendekripsi. Untuk akses lintas akun, secret harus dienkripsi dengan customer managed key yang key policy-nya mengizinkan role akun B melakukan kms:Decrypt, ditambah resource policy pada secret dan IAM policy di akun B. Replikasi multi-Region menyalin secret ke Region lain di akun yang sama, bukan ke akun lain. Menyalin nilai ke Parameter Store di akun B membuat duplikasi password yang tidak ikut rotasi. Aturan umum: akses lintas akun ke secret = resource policy secret + customer managed KMS key dengan key policy lintas akun + IAM policy di akun konsumen.","r":["Salah — Key policy AWS managed key tidak dapat diedit oleh pelanggan.","Benar — Customer managed key dengan key policy lintas akun memungkinkan role di akun B mendekripsi secret.","Salah — Replikasi Secrets Manager hanya ke Region lain dalam akun yang sama.","Salah — Salinan manual tidak ikut rotasi dan menambah risiko kebocoran."],"k":"Tips ujian: secret lintas akun → wajib customer managed KMS key (aws/secretsmanager tidak bisa dipakai lintas akun)."},{"id":"E2A-57","d":2,"ts":"2.1.8","t":"Vector index types: HNSW vs IVF","q":"A company is building a semantic search feature over 5 million document embeddings. New documents are added continuously throughout the day. The application requires the highest possible recall and the lowest query latency, and the company has enough memory budget to hold the index in memory. Which vector index type should a data engineer choose?","o":["IVF (inverted file index), because it partitions vectors into clusters that must be trained on a data sample before indexing","Flat (brute-force) index, because it compares the query against every vector","An inverted text index on the document titles","HNSW (Hierarchical Navigable Small Worlds), because it builds a multi-layer proximity graph that supports fast, high-recall approximate searches and incremental inserts"],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci adalah 'highest possible recall', 'lowest query latency', 'enough memory budget', dan 'added continuously'. HNSW membangun graph berlapis: lapisan atas berisi sedikit node untuk navigasi cepat, lapisan bawah berisi semua node, sehingga pencarian approximate nearest neighbor sangat cepat dengan recall tinggi; vektor baru bisa disisipkan secara inkremental tanpa pelatihan ulang. Konsekuensinya, HNSW memakai memori lebih besar, yang di sini tidak menjadi kendala. Distraktor terdekat adalah IVF: membagi vektor ke cluster (centroid) dan hanya mencari di beberapa cluster terdekat, lebih hemat memori, tetapi memerlukan langkah training dan recall-nya bergantung pada jumlah cluster yang diperiksa; distribusi data baru dapat menurunkan kualitas cluster. Flat memberi hasil eksak, tetapi latensi tinggi pada 5 juta vektor. Aturan umum: HNSW = recall dan kecepatan terbaik dengan memori lebih besar; IVF = lebih hemat memori, perlu training, trade-off recall.","r":["Salah — IVF memerlukan training dan biasanya memiliki trade-off recall/latensi yang lebih buruk daripada HNSW ketika memori bukan kendala.","Salah — Flat menghitung jarak ke semua vektor sehingga latensinya tinggi pada 5 juta vektor.","Salah — Inverted text index untuk pencarian kata kunci, bukan similarity search pada embedding.","Benar — HNSW memberi recall tinggi dan latensi rendah, mendukung penyisipan inkremental, dengan biaya memori lebih besar yang masih dalam anggaran."],"k":"Highest recall + lowest latency + memory OK → HNSW; memory-constrained at huge scale → IVF (needs training)."},{"id":"E1A-45","d":1,"ts":"1.1.7","t":"Lambda event filtering","q":"A Kinesis data stream carries several event types, but an AWS Lambda function only needs to process records whose JSON payload has eventType equal to 'purchase'. Currently the function is invoked for every record and discards most of them. The team wants to reduce Lambda cost with the LEAST code change. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Create a second Kinesis data stream and modify the producers to send purchase events to it.","Add an event filtering pattern to the Kinesis event source mapping that matches records where data.eventType is 'purchase'.","Use an Amazon Data Firehose stream with a Lambda transformation to drop non-purchase events.","Increase the batch size so that more records are discarded per invocation."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: hanya butuh record dengan 'eventType = purchase', ingin mengurangi biaya Lambda dengan 'LEAST code change'. Event source mapping Lambda untuk Kinesis mendukung event filtering: Lambda mengevaluasi pola filter pada payload JSON (field data) sebelum memanggil fungsi, sehingga record yang tidak cocok tidak memicu invocation dan tidak ditagih. Distraktor terdekat adalah membuat stream kedua: berhasil, tetapi menuntut perubahan di semua producer. Firehose dengan transformasi Lambda tetap memanggil Lambda untuk setiap record dan mengubah arsitektur. Menaikkan batch size mengurangi invocation, tetapi tetap membuang-buang komputasi untuk record yang tidak relevan. Aturan umum: memfilter record sebelum Lambda dipanggil = event filtering pada event source mapping.","r":["Salah — Memerlukan perubahan pada semua producer dan stream tambahan.","Benar — Event filtering mencegah invocation untuk record yang tidak cocok tanpa mengubah kode fungsi.","Salah — Transformasi Lambda di Firehose tetap memproses setiap record dan menambah komponen.","Salah — Record yang tidak relevan tetap dibaca dan diproses oleh fungsi."],"k":"Lambda hanya untuk sebagian record → event filtering pada event source mapping."},{"id":"E1A-65","d":1,"ts":"1.1.11","t":"Designing replayable pipelines","q":"A company ingests clickstream data with Amazon Data Firehose, which invokes an AWS Lambda function to transform records before delivering them to Amazon S3. The company wants to be able to rebuild the curated dataset at any time in the future if the transformation logic changes. Which TWO design choices support this replayability requirement? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Delete raw records after the transformation succeeds to reduce storage costs.","Enable Firehose source record backup to Amazon S3 so that the untransformed records are kept in addition to the transformed output.","Overwrite the curated dataset in place without keeping any copy of the original records.","Rely on the Firehose buffer to retain records for later reprocessing.","Store raw data in an immutable raw zone in Amazon S3 and build curated datasets from it with idempotent, re-runnable jobs."],"a":[1,4],"e":"Kata kunci: 'rebuild the curated dataset at any time in the future' jika 'transformation logic changes'. Replayability membutuhkan salinan data asli yang tahan lama dan pipeline yang bisa dijalankan ulang. Firehose source record backup menyimpan record asli (sebelum transformasi Lambda) ke S3 di samping output yang sudah ditransformasi. Arsitektur data lake dengan raw zone yang immutable, ditambah job yang idempotent, memungkinkan dataset curated dibangun ulang kapan saja tanpa duplikasi. Distraktor terdekat adalah mengandalkan buffer Firehose: buffer hanya menahan data beberapa menit sebelum dikirim dan bukan penyimpanan untuk replay. Menghapus raw data atau menimpa dataset tanpa salinan asli menghilangkan kemampuan replay. Aturan umum: simpan data mentah secara immutable (S3 raw zone) dan buat transformasi deterministik/idempotent.","r":["Salah — Menghapus data mentah menghilangkan kemampuan replay.","Benar — Source record backup menyimpan record asli sebelum transformasi sehingga dapat diproses ulang.","Salah — Tanpa salinan data asli, dataset tidak dapat dibangun ulang dengan logika baru.","Salah — Buffer Firehose hanya menahan data sementara sebelum delivery, bukan penyimpanan untuk replay.","Benar — Raw zone immutable + job idempotent memungkinkan dataset curated dibangun ulang kapan saja."],"k":"Replayability → simpan raw data immutable (S3 raw zone, Firehose source record backup) + job idempotent."},{"id":"E1C-57","d":1,"ts":"1.4.4","t":"Version control and secrets best practices","q":"A data team stores AWS Glue job scripts and SQL transformations. Currently, engineers edit scripts directly in the production Glue console, and database passwords are passed as plaintext job parameters. The team wants to adopt software engineering best practices. Which combination of actions should the team take? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Store all scripts in a Git repository, develop on feature branches, and merge to main only through reviewed pull requests that run automated tests.","Allow every engineer to push directly to main so that changes reach production faster.","Store database credentials in AWS Secrets Manager and retrieve them at runtime by using the job's IAM role.","Commit a configuration file that contains the database passwords to the repository so all environments use the same values.","Keep editing scripts in the Glue console but download a copy weekly as a backup."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Dua masalah: perubahan langsung di konsol produksi (tanpa kontrol versi dan review) dan 'passwords ... as plaintext job parameters'. Praktik terbaik adalah menyimpan kode di Git dengan feature branch dan pull request yang direview serta menjalankan tes otomatis sebelum merge, sehingga setiap perubahan terlacak, bisa di-rollback, dan terverifikasi. Kredensial disimpan di AWS Secrets Manager dan diambil saat runtime melalui IAM role job, sehingga tidak muncul di parameter, log, atau repositori. Distractor terdekat adalah push langsung ke main: lebih cepat, tetapi tanpa review dan tes. Menyimpan password di repo membocorkan rahasia ke semua orang yang punya akses. Unduhan mingguan bukan kontrol versi. Aturan umum: kode di Git dengan PR + CI; rahasia di Secrets Manager, tidak pernah di kode atau parameter.","r":["Benar — Git dengan feature branch, PR review, dan tes otomatis memberi keterlacakan dan kualitas.","Salah — Melewati review dan tes meningkatkan risiko bug di produksi.","Benar — Secrets Manager menyimpan kredensial secara aman dan diambil saat runtime lewat IAM role.","Salah — Rahasia di repositori mudah bocor dan sulit dirotasi.","Salah — Salinan mingguan bukan kontrol versi dan perubahan tetap tanpa review."],"k":"Tips ujian: best practice → Git + PR + automated tests; credentials → Secrets Manager."},{"id":"E4B-46","d":4,"ts":"4.5.3","t":"SCP Region restriction","q":"A European company uses AWS Organizations. A new data privacy policy states that no data, including backups and replicas, may be stored in AWS Regions outside eu-central-1 and eu-west-1. Administrators in member accounts have broad IAM permissions. The company needs a preventive control that cannot be bypassed by member account administrators. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Attach a service control policy (SCP) to the organization root or relevant OUs that denies actions when aws:RequestedRegion is not eu-central-1 or eu-west-1, with exceptions for required global services.","Attach an IAM policy to every IAM user and role in each member account that denies actions outside the two Regions.","Deploy an AWS Config rule that reports resources created outside the approved Regions.","Enable S3 Block Public Access at the organization level."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: 'preventive control' yang 'cannot be bypassed by member account administrators' untuk membatasi Region. SCP di AWS Organizations menetapkan batas izin maksimum bagi semua principal di akun anggota, termasuk administrator; deny dengan condition aws:RequestedRegion di luar daftar Region yang diizinkan mencegah pembuatan resource, backup, atau replika di Region lain. Global services (misalnya IAM, Organizations, CloudFront, Route 53) biasanya dikecualikan agar tidak rusak. Distraktor terdekat adalah IAM policy di setiap principal: admin akun dapat melepas atau mengubahnya, dan sulit dipelihara. AWS Config rule bersifat detektif, hanya melaporkan setelah resource dibuat. S3 Block Public Access mencegah akses publik, bukan membatasi Region. Aturan umum: pembatasan Region yang tidak bisa dilewati admin akun → SCP dengan aws:RequestedRegion.","r":["Benar — SCP dengan aws:RequestedRegion mencegah aksi di Region yang tidak diizinkan dan tidak bisa dilewati admin akun anggota.","Salah — Admin akun dapat mengubah atau menghapus IAM policy, dan pemeliharaannya berat.","Salah — Config rule hanya mendeteksi setelah kejadian, bukan mencegah.","Salah — Block Public Access mengatur akses publik, bukan lokasi Region data."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'prevent use of non-approved Regions org-wide' → SCP + aws:RequestedRegion (preventive); Config = detective."},{"id":"E3B-22","d":3,"ts":"3.3.7","t":"CloudWatch Logs retention","q":"A data engineer notices that the CloudWatch Logs storage bill keeps increasing. Most log groups created by AWS Glue, Lambda, and Amazon EMR use the default settings, and the company only needs these logs for 30 days. Which action will reduce the cost with the LEAST effort?","o":["Delete the log groups every month and allow the services to recreate them.","Set a retention policy of 30 days on each log group.","Export all log groups to Amazon S3 every day and delete the exported events manually.","Enable KMS encryption on the log groups."],"a":[1],"e":"Penyebabnya: retensi default log group CloudWatch Logs adalah 'Never expire', sehingga data menumpuk dan biaya penyimpanan terus naik. Persyaratan 'only needs these logs for 30 days' dipenuhi dengan menetapkan retention policy 30 hari (PutRetentionPolicy) per log group; CloudWatch akan menghapus event lama secara otomatis. Distraktor terdekat adalah menghapus log group tiap bulan — kasar, berisiko menghapus log yang masih dibutuhkan, dan butuh kerja manual berulang. Ekspor harian ke S3 menambah pekerjaan dan tidak menghapus data dari CloudWatch. Enkripsi KMS tidak mengurangi volume. Aturan: biaya log naik terus → cek retensi 'Never expire'.","r":["Salah — Penghapusan manual bulanan berisiko kehilangan log yang masih dalam periode 30 hari dan butuh kerja berulang.","Benar — Retention policy 30 hari membuat CloudWatch menghapus log lama secara otomatis.","Salah — Ekspor dan penghapusan manual menambah pekerjaan dan biaya tanpa perlu.","Salah — Enkripsi tidak mengurangi jumlah data yang disimpan."],"k":"Tips ujian: default retensi CloudWatch Logs = never expire → set retention policy."},{"id":"E4A-58","d":4,"ts":"4.2.6","t":"Permissions boundaries for delegated administration","q":"A data platform team wants senior data engineers to create IAM roles for their own AWS Glue jobs without waiting for the security team. The security team must ensure that no role created by the engineers can ever have more permissions than a predefined set (Glue, specific S3 buckets, and CloudWatch Logs), and that engineers cannot remove this restriction. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Allow iam:CreateRole and iam:AttachRolePolicy for the engineers and review new roles weekly with AWS Config.","Give the engineers the IAMFullAccess managed policy and ask them to follow a written guideline.","Create a service-linked role for AWS Glue and let the engineers attach policies to it.","Create a permissions boundary policy with the predefined permissions, and allow iam:CreateRole only when the iam:PermissionsBoundary condition key equals that policy's ARN, while denying changes to or removal of the boundary."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci: 'never ... more permissions than a predefined set' dan 'cannot remove this restriction'. Permissions boundary menentukan izin maksimum yang dapat dimiliki sebuah role; izin efektif adalah irisan antara identity-based policy dan boundary. Dengan mengizinkan iam:CreateRole hanya jika kondisi iam:PermissionsBoundary sama dengan ARN boundary, setiap role baru wajib memakai batas tersebut. Menolak iam:DeleteRolePermissionsBoundary dan perubahan pada policy boundary mencegah engineer menghapus batasan. Review mingguan dengan AWS Config hanya bersifat detektif, bukan preventif. IAMFullAccess dengan pedoman tertulis tidak ditegakkan teknis. Service-linked role tidak dapat diberi policy tambahan oleh pelanggan. Aturan umum: delegasi pembuatan role tanpa privilege escalation → permissions boundary + kondisi iam:PermissionsBoundary.","r":["Salah — Kontrol detektif mingguan tidak mencegah role dengan izin berlebih dibuat dan dipakai.","Salah — Pedoman tertulis tidak ditegakkan dan IAMFullAccess memungkinkan eskalasi privilege.","Salah — Service-linked role tidak bisa diedit atau ditambah policy oleh pelanggan.","Benar — Boundary wajib pada setiap role baru dan proteksi terhadap penghapusan mencegah eskalasi privilege."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'delegate role creation safely' → permissions boundary + kondisi iam:PermissionsBoundary pada CreateRole."},{"id":"E1C-71","d":1,"ts":"1.4.6","t":"SAM gradual deployments","q":"A Lambda function that transforms incoming records is deployed with AWS SAM. The team wants new versions to receive 10% of traffic for 5 minutes, then all traffic if no errors occur, and to roll back automatically if a CloudWatch alarm on function errors fires. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST effort?","o":["Manually create two aliases and edit their weights in the Lambda console after each deployment.","Deploy each new version as a separate function and change the trigger to point to it.","Add AutoPublishAlias and a DeploymentPreference with type Canary10Percent5Minutes and the error alarm to the function in the SAM template.","Use reserved concurrency to send 10% of traffic to the new version."],"a":[2],"e":"Kebutuhannya: '10% of traffic for 5 minutes', lalu penuh jika aman, dan 'roll back automatically' berdasarkan alarm, dengan 'LEAST effort'. Di SAM, AutoPublishAlias menerbitkan versi baru dan memperbarui alias, sedangkan DeploymentPreference (misalnya Canary10Percent5Minutes) memakai AWS CodeDeploy untuk menggeser trafik secara bertahap dan rollback otomatis jika alarm CloudWatch yang dicantumkan berbunyi; hooks pre/post traffic juga bisa ditambahkan. Distractor terdekat adalah mengatur bobot alias secara manual: mekanismenya sama, tetapi manual dan tanpa rollback otomatis. Membuat fungsi terpisah tidak memberi pergeseran trafik bertahap. Reserved concurrency membatasi concurrency, bukan membagi trafik antar versi. Aturan umum: canary/linear deployment untuk Lambda → SAM DeploymentPreference (CodeDeploy) + alarms.","r":["Salah — Proses manual tanpa rollback otomatis.","Salah — Tidak ada pergeseran trafik bertahap atau rollback otomatis.","Benar — DeploymentPreference memakai CodeDeploy untuk canary dan rollback otomatis berdasarkan alarm.","Salah — Reserved concurrency tidak membagi trafik antar versi."],"k":"Tips ujian: SAM canary + auto rollback → AutoPublishAlias + DeploymentPreference (CodeDeploy) + Alarms."},{"id":"E2A-33","d":2,"ts":"2.1.4","t":"Transfer Family managed workflows","q":"Partners upload PGP-encrypted files to an AWS Transfer Family SFTP server that stores files in Amazon S3. After each upload, every file must be decrypted, copied to a processing prefix, and tagged with the partner name before downstream jobs run. The company wants to minimize custom code and use processing steps that are built into the transfer service, with execution logs for each file. What should a data engineer do?","o":["Configure an S3 event notification that invokes an AWS Lambda function to decrypt, copy, and tag each file.","Configure a Transfer Family managed workflow with decrypt, copy, and tag steps that runs on upload completion.","Schedule an AWS Glue job every 15 minutes to scan the upload prefix and process new files.","Ask the partners to send unencrypted files and use S3 default encryption."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci adalah langkah pasca-unggah 'decrypted, copied ... and tagged', 'minimize custom code', dan langkah yang 'built into the transfer service'. Transfer Family managed workflows menyediakan langkah bawaan seperti decrypt (PGP), copy, tag, dan delete, serta langkah kustom berbasis Lambda bila perlu; workflow dipicu otomatis saat unggahan selesai, dan setiap eksekusi dapat dipantau melalui log dan metrik Amazon CloudWatch. Distraktor terdekat adalah S3 event + Lambda: bisa dikerjakan, tetapi seluruh logika dekripsi, copy, tag, dan penanganan error harus ditulis sendiri. Glue terjadwal menambah latensi dan kode. Meminta file tanpa enkripsi melemahkan keamanan data dari partner. Aturan umum: proses pasca-unggah standar di Transfer Family (decrypt/copy/tag/delete) → managed workflows.","r":["Salah — Bisa bekerja, tetapi semua logika dekripsi, copy, dan tag harus ditulis dan dipelihara sendiri di luar Transfer Family.","Benar — Managed workflow menyediakan langkah decrypt, copy, dan tag bawaan yang berjalan otomatis setelah unggahan, dengan log eksekusi per file di Amazon CloudWatch.","Salah — Glue terjadwal menambah keterlambatan hingga 15 menit dan memerlukan kode kustom untuk dekripsi PGP.","Salah — Menghapus enkripsi PGP menurunkan keamanan dan mengubah persyaratan partner; S3 default encryption hanya melindungi data at rest."],"k":"Post-upload processing (decrypt/copy/tag) in Transfer Family → managed workflows."},{"id":"E4A-11","d":4,"ts":"4.1.3","t":"RDS managed master password in Secrets Manager","q":"A data team is creating a new Amazon RDS for MySQL DB instance for a pipeline. The security team requires that the master user password never be known by any person, be stored encrypted, and be rotated automatically. The team wants the LEAST operational overhead. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Generate a random password, store it in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store as a SecureString, and write a Lambda function that rotates it.","Enable the RDS integration with AWS Secrets Manager so that RDS generates the master user password, stores it in a Secrets Manager secret, and manages its rotation.","Enable IAM database authentication and remove the master user from the DB instance.","Create the DB instance with a password supplied in an AWS CloudFormation template parameter marked NoEcho."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: 'never be known by any person', 'rotated automatically', 'LEAST operational overhead'. Amazon RDS (dan Aurora) punya integrasi bawaan dengan Secrets Manager untuk master user: RDS membuat password, menyimpannya di secret yang dienkripsi KMS, dan mengelola rotasinya (default 7 hari) tanpa Lambda rotasi yang perlu Anda kelola. Tidak ada orang yang perlu melihat password karena aplikasi mengambilnya dari secret. Opsi Parameter Store dengan Lambda custom bisa berfungsi, tetapi overhead-nya jauh lebih tinggi. IAM database authentication bagus untuk user aplikasi, tetapi master user tidak bisa dihapus dari instance. NoEcho hanya menyembunyikan nilai di console CloudFormation; password tetap diketahui pembuat template dan tidak dirotasi. Aturan umum: master password RDS/Aurora → aktifkan 'managed in Secrets Manager'.","r":["Salah — Berfungsi, tetapi membangun dan memelihara rotasi custom menambah overhead.","Benar — Integrasi RDS dengan Secrets Manager menghasilkan, menyimpan terenkripsi, dan merotasi password master secara otomatis.","Salah — Master user tidak bisa dihapus, dan IAM authentication tidak menggantikan kebutuhan pengelolaan password master.","Salah — NoEcho hanya menyembunyikan tampilan parameter; password tetap diketahui manusia dan tidak dirotasi."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'master password managed by RDS' → integrasi RDS/Aurora dengan Secrets Manager (ManageMasterUserPassword)."},{"id":"E1C-80","d":1,"ts":"1.4.11","t":"Tree structures and recursive CTEs","q":"An Amazon Redshift table product_category stores a category hierarchy with the columns category_id and parent_category_id, where root categories have a NULL parent. The hierarchy depth varies from 2 to 8 levels. An analyst needs all descendant categories of 'Electronics' at any depth in a single SQL query. Which approach meets this requirement?","o":["Join the table to itself exactly twice.","Use a window function with PARTITION BY parent_category_id.","Use GROUP BY parent_category_id with a HAVING clause.","Use a recursive common table expression (WITH RECURSIVE) that starts from the 'Electronics' row and repeatedly joins children to the previous level."],"a":[3],"e":"Data ini berbentuk struktur tree (setiap kategori punya satu parent, dan root ber-parent NULL) dengan kedalaman bervariasi 2 hingga 8 level, sedangkan kebutuhannya adalah 'all descendant categories ... at any depth in a single SQL query'. Recursive CTE (WITH RECURSIVE), yang didukung Amazon Redshift, memulai dari node anchor 'Electronics' lalu berulang kali menggabungkan baris anak ke hasil level sebelumnya sampai tidak ada anak baru, sehingga menelusuri seluruh subtree berapa pun kedalamannya. Distractor terdekat adalah self-join dua kali: hanya menjangkau dua level dan gagal untuk kedalaman hingga 8. Window function dan GROUP BY hanya bekerja pada satu level hubungan parent-anak. Aturan umum: hierarki/tree dengan kedalaman variabel di SQL → recursive CTE.","r":["Salah — Self-join tetap hanya mencapai kedalaman yang ditentukan, bukan hingga 8 level.","Salah — Window function bekerja pada partisi baris, bukan menelusuri hierarki.","Salah — GROUP BY hanya mengelompokkan anak langsung, bukan semua keturunan.","Benar — Recursive CTE menelusuri tree dari node awal sampai seluruh keturunan ditemukan."],"k":"Tips ujian: hierarchy/tree dengan kedalaman bervariasi di SQL → WITH RECURSIVE (recursive CTE)."},{"id":"E3B-58","d":3,"ts":"3.4.3","t":"Redshift constraints and consistent loads","q":"A data engineer declared customer_id as the PRIMARY KEY of an Amazon Redshift dimension table. After the nightly load was rerun twice because of a failure, reports show doubled revenue for some customers. Investigation shows duplicate customer_id rows in the table. What is the cause, and how should the engineer keep the table consistent?","o":["The PRIMARY KEY was dropped by the failed load; recreate it so that Redshift rejects duplicates.","Redshift does not enforce PRIMARY KEY constraints; load the data into a staging table and use a MERGE (or delete-then-insert) operation into the target so that reruns are idempotent.","Run VACUUM to remove the duplicate rows automatically.","Change the table's distribution style to ALL to prevent duplicates."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'declared customer_id as the PRIMARY KEY' tetapi tetap ada duplikat setelah 'rerun twice'. Di Amazon Redshift, constraint PRIMARY KEY, UNIQUE, dan FOREIGN KEY hanya bersifat informasional (dipakai optimizer) dan TIDAK ditegakkan, sehingga load ulang menyisipkan baris yang sama lagi. Solusinya adalah load yang idempoten: muat ke staging table lalu gunakan MERGE atau delete-then-insert dalam satu transaksi ke tabel target. Distraktor terdekat adalah membuat ulang PRIMARY KEY — tidak akan menolak duplikat karena tetap tidak ditegakkan. VACUUM merapikan baris terhapus, bukan duplikat. DISTSTYLE ALL hanya mengatur distribusi data. Aturan: Redshift tidak menegakkan constraint → pastikan konsistensi di pipeline (staging + MERGE).","r":["Salah — Meskipun dibuat ulang, PRIMARY KEY di Redshift tidak menolak duplikat.","Benar — Constraint tidak ditegakkan, jadi load harus idempoten melalui staging table dan MERGE.","Salah — VACUUM tidak mendeteksi atau menghapus baris duplikat.","Salah — Gaya distribusi tidak memengaruhi keunikan data."],"k":"Tips ujian: Redshift PK/FK/UNIQUE = informational only → dedupe dengan staging + MERGE."},{"id":"E3B-11","d":3,"ts":"3.3.2","t":"Step Functions logging for traceability","q":"A company runs high-volume AWS Step Functions Express Workflows that orchestrate data validation Lambda functions. For traceability, the operations team must be able to see the input and output of every state for any execution after it completes. Which solution meets this requirement?","o":["Use the Step Functions console execution history, which records every state transition for Express Workflows for 90 days.","Enable CloudWatch Logs logging for the state machine with the log level set to ALL and include execution data.","Enable a CloudTrail trail with management events to record each state transition.","Enable AWS X-Ray tracing on the state machine to store the state input and output payloads."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'Express Workflows' dan 'input and output of every state'. Berbeda dengan Standard Workflows yang punya execution history di service, Express Workflows tidak menyimpan riwayat eksekusi detail di Step Functions; riwayatnya harus dikirim ke CloudWatch Logs. Dengan logging level ALL dan includeExecutionData, setiap event state beserta input/output tercatat di log group. Distraktor terdekat adalah console execution history, tetapi fitur 90 hari itu berlaku untuk Standard Workflows. CloudTrail hanya mencatat panggilan API seperti StartExecution, bukan transisi state. X-Ray (di luar cakupan ujian) menelusuri latensi, bukan menyimpan payload. Aturan: Express Workflow + observability → CloudWatch Logs.","r":["Salah — Riwayat eksekusi detail di console berlaku untuk Standard Workflows, bukan Express.","Benar — Logging ALL dengan execution data mencatat input/output setiap state ke CloudWatch Logs untuk penelusuran.","Salah — CloudTrail mencatat panggilan API, bukan setiap transisi state di dalam eksekusi.","Salah — X-Ray berfokus pada tracing latensi antar layanan, bukan audit payload state, dan X-Ray di luar cakupan ujian."],"k":"Tips ujian: Step Functions Express → history hanya lewat CloudWatch Logs (level ALL + includeExecutionData)."},{"id":"E2A-22","d":2,"ts":"2.1.3","t":"Purpose-built databases: DocumentDB","q":"A company runs a content management application on a self-managed MongoDB cluster. Documents are semi-structured JSON with nested fields, and the application uses MongoDB drivers and queries. The company wants a fully managed AWS database with minimal application changes. Which data store should a data engineer choose?","o":["Amazon DynamoDB","Amazon Keyspaces (for Apache Cassandra)","Amazon Neptune","Amazon DocumentDB (with MongoDB compatibility)"],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci adalah 'semi-structured JSON', 'MongoDB drivers and queries', dan 'minimal application changes'. Amazon DocumentDB adalah database dokumen fully managed yang kompatibel dengan API MongoDB, sehingga aplikasi bisa tetap memakai driver dan query MongoDB yang ada. Distraktor terdekat adalah DynamoDB: bisa menyimpan dokumen JSON, tetapi API-nya berbeda sehingga aplikasi harus ditulis ulang. Keyspaces kompatibel dengan Cassandra (CQL), bukan MongoDB, dan Neptune adalah graph database. Aturan umum: pemetaan engine open-source ke layanan managed AWS — MongoDB → DocumentDB, Cassandra → Keyspaces, Redis → MemoryDB, graph → Neptune.","r":["Salah — DynamoDB memakai API sendiri; driver dan query MongoDB harus diganti.","Salah — Keyspaces kompatibel dengan Apache Cassandra (CQL), bukan MongoDB.","Salah — Neptune adalah graph database untuk data relasi antar-entitas, bukan document store MongoDB.","Benar — DocumentDB kompatibel dengan MongoDB sehingga aplikasi bisa pindah ke layanan managed dengan perubahan minimal."],"k":"MongoDB-compatible managed document DB → Amazon DocumentDB."},{"id":"E3A-34","d":3,"ts":"3.1.9","t":"EventBridge Scheduler","q":"A data team in Sydney must start an AWS Glue workflow at 02:00 local time every day. Sydney observes daylight saving time, and the team does not want to update UTC cron expressions twice a year. The team also needs to schedule a one-time backfill run next Saturday at 22:00 local time. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Create Amazon EventBridge Scheduler schedules: a recurring cron schedule and a one-time schedule, both using the Australia/Sydney time zone, with the workflow start as the target.","Create two Amazon EventBridge rules with UTC cron expressions and update them manually when daylight saving time starts and ends.","Run a cron job on an Amazon EC2 instance configured with the Australia/Sydney time zone.","Create an AWS Lambda function that runs every hour, checks the local time, and starts the workflow at 02:00."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'local time', 'daylight saving time', 'not update UTC cron twice a year', dan 'one-time backfill'. Amazon EventBridge Scheduler mendukung zona waktu (misalnya Australia/Sydney) dan menyesuaikan daylight saving time secara otomatis, serta mendukung jadwal one-time dengan ekspresi at(). Scheduler juga bisa langsung memanggil ribuan API AWS sebagai target universal, termasuk memulai Glue workflow. Rule terjadwal EventBridge yang lama hanya memakai UTC, sehingga perlu diubah manual setiap pergantian DST. EC2 cron menambah server yang harus dikelola. Lambda per jam yang mengecek waktu adalah kode tambahan dan pemborosan invocation. Aturan umum: jadwal dengan time zone, DST, atau one-time → EventBridge Scheduler.","r":["Benar — EventBridge Scheduler mendukung time zone dengan DST otomatis dan jadwal one-time, tanpa kode.","Salah — Rule terjadwal memakai UTC sehingga harus diperbarui manual setiap pergantian DST.","Salah — EC2 harus dikelola, di-patch, dan menjadi single point of failure.","Salah — Kode tambahan dan invocation per jam yang tidak perlu."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'time zone / DST / one-time schedule' → EventBridge Scheduler (bukan scheduled rule UTC)."},{"id":"E4B-34","d":4,"ts":"4.4.4","t":"Athena for log analysis in S3","q":"A company stores several terabytes of Application Load Balancer access logs per month in Amazon S3 as compressed text files. Analysts run a few SQL queries each month to investigate traffic patterns, usually filtering by date. The company wants the MOST cost-effective solution with minimal infrastructure to manage. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Load the logs into an Amazon OpenSearch Service domain and query them with OpenSearch Dashboards.","Create an Amazon Athena table over the log location and use Athena CTAS queries to convert the data to Parquet partitioned by date, then run the monthly queries on the Parquet table.","Use CloudWatch Logs Insights to query the S3 log files.","Create an Amazon Redshift provisioned cluster and COPY the logs into it every day."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: 'a few SQL queries each month', 'filtering by date', 'MOST cost-effective', dan 'minimal infrastructure'. Athena serverless dibayar per data yang dipindai sehingga cocok untuk query jarang atas data di S3; mengonversi log ke Parquet yang dipartisi tanggal dengan CTAS mengurangi data yang dipindai secara drastis (kolumnar, terkompresi, partition pruning). Distraktor terdekat adalah OpenSearch: cocok untuk pencarian real-time, tetapi domain harus berjalan terus sehingga mahal untuk beberapa query per bulan. Logs Insights hanya meng-query data di CloudWatch Logs, bukan file di S3. Cluster Redshift yang selalu aktif dan pipeline COPY harian berlebihan untuk pola query ini. Aturan umum: query log di S3 yang jarang → Athena, optimalkan dengan Parquet + partisi.","r":["Salah — Domain OpenSearch harus berjalan terus, mahal untuk query bulanan yang jarang.","Benar — Athena serverless + Parquet berpartisi tanggal meminimalkan biaya dan infrastruktur.","Salah — CloudWatch Logs Insights tidak dapat meng-query file di Amazon S3.","Salah — Cluster Redshift dan pipeline harian berlebihan untuk beberapa query per bulan."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'infrequent SQL on logs in S3, cost-effective' → Athena (+ Parquet/partitions)."},{"id":"E1A-21","d":1,"ts":"1.1.3","t":"AWS DataSync task options","q":"A company uses AWS DataSync to copy files nightly from an on-premises NFS share to Amazon S3. Recently, some transfers continued into business hours and saturated the company's internet link. The company needs transfers to avoid affecting business users while still completing each night. Which configuration change should the data engineer make?","o":["Replace DataSync with an AWS Snowball Edge device every night.","Configure a bandwidth limit on the DataSync task and schedule the task to start earlier in the evening.","Enable Amazon S3 Transfer Acceleration on the destination bucket.","Change the task to transfer all data instead of only changed data."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: transfer 'saturated the company's internet link' saat jam kerja, tetapi tetap harus 'completing each night'. DataSync task mendukung pengaturan bandwidth limit (throttle) sehingga transfer tidak menghabiskan seluruh link, dan jadwal task bisa dimajukan agar selesai sebelum jam kerja. Distraktor terdekat adalah S3 Transfer Acceleration: itu fitur untuk upload langsung ke S3 lewat edge location, tidak membatasi pemakaian bandwidth lokal dan tidak dipakai oleh DataSync agent. Snowball Edge setiap malam tidak realistis secara operasional. Mentransfer seluruh data justru menambah volume. Aturan umum: DataSync mengganggu jaringan = gunakan bandwidth limit dan atur jadwal; DataSync secara default hanya mentransfer data yang berubah.","r":["Salah — Mengirim perangkat fisik setiap malam tidak praktis, dan Snowball Edge kini tidak tersedia untuk pelanggan baru.","Benar — Bandwidth limit melindungi link perusahaan dan jadwal lebih awal memastikan transfer selesai malam itu.","Salah — Transfer Acceleration tidak membatasi bandwidth lokal dan tidak relevan untuk DataSync agent.","Salah — Transfer semua data menambah volume dan memperburuk masalah."],"k":"DataSync menghabiskan bandwidth → set bandwidth limit pada task + atur schedule."},{"id":"E2A-11","d":2,"ts":"2.1.2","t":"Redshift distribution styles","q":"A data engineer is designing tables in Amazon Redshift. The sales fact table has 4 billion rows and is joined in almost every query to the customer dimension table (50 million rows) on customer_id. Five other dimension tables have fewer than 5,000 rows each and change rarely. Which distribution design minimizes data redistribution during joins?","o":["Use DISTSTYLE ALL for every table, including the fact table.","Use DISTSTYLE KEY on customer_id for both the sales fact table and the customer table, and DISTSTYLE ALL for the small dimension tables.","Use DISTSTYLE EVEN for all tables so data is spread equally across slices.","Use DISTSTYLE KEY on order_date for the sales fact table and DISTSTYLE ALL for the customer table."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci adalah 'joined in almost every query ... on customer_id' dan 'minimizes data redistribution'. Jika fact table dan customer table sama-sama didistribusikan dengan KEY pada kolom join customer_id, baris yang cocok berada di slice yang sama sehingga join terjadi lokal tanpa redistribusi (collocated join). Tabel dimensi kecil yang jarang berubah ideal memakai DISTSTYLE ALL karena salinan penuh ada di setiap node. Distraktor terdekat adalah KEY pada order_date dengan customer ALL: menyalin 50 juta baris ke setiap node memboroskan storage dan memperlambat load, dan order_date bukan kolom join. DISTSTYLE EVEN menyebabkan redistribusi setiap kali join. Aturan umum: KEY pada kolom join untuk dua tabel besar yang sering di-join, ALL untuk dimensi kecil yang jarang berubah.","r":["Salah — Menyalin fact table 4 miliar baris ke semua node memboroskan storage dan memperlambat load secara drastis.","Benar — KEY pada customer_id menghasilkan collocated join untuk dua tabel besar, dan ALL cocok untuk dimensi kecil yang stabil.","Salah — EVEN menyebar data rata tetapi memaksa redistribusi atau broadcast saat join pada customer_id.","Salah — order_date bukan kolom join, dan ALL untuk tabel 50 juta baris mahal untuk storage dan maintenance."],"k":"Large-to-large join → DISTKEY sama pada kolom join; small static dimensions → DISTSTYLE ALL."},{"id":"E3A-11","d":3,"ts":"3.1.3","t":"SDK retries and throttling","q":"A data ingestion application calls AWS service APIs through the AWS SDK at a high rate. During peak periods, some calls fail with ThrottlingException errors, and the current code immediately resends failed calls in a tight loop, which makes the problem worse. The data engineer wants a fix that requires minimal code changes. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Configure the SDK client to use the standard or adaptive retry mode with a higher maximum number of attempts, which retries with exponential backoff and jitter.","Remove all retries so that throttled requests fail fast and are logged.","Create a separate SDK client for every request so that each call has its own rate limit.","Move the application to a different AWS Region whenever throttling occurs."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'ThrottlingException', 'retry in a tight loop makes the problem worse', dan 'minimal code changes'. AWS SDK sudah punya mekanisme retry bawaan; dengan retry mode 'standard' atau 'adaptive' (misalnya melalui konfigurasi retries di botocore Config), panggilan yang di-throttle diulang dengan exponential backoff dan jitter. Mode adaptive juga menambahkan rate limiting di sisi klien. Ini mengurangi tekanan ke API dan cukup diubah lewat konfigurasi. Menghapus retry membuat data gagal masuk. Membuat client baru tidak menambah kuota karena kuota berlaku per akun/Region, bukan per client. Pindah Region menambah kompleksitas dan masalah residensi data. Aturan umum: throttling → exponential backoff dengan jitter, idealnya memakai retry bawaan SDK.","r":["Benar — Retry mode standard/adaptive di SDK memberi exponential backoff dan jitter hanya lewat konfigurasi.","Salah — Tanpa retry, permintaan yang di-throttle gagal permanen dan data hilang.","Salah — Kuota API berlaku per akun dan Region, bukan per objek client.","Salah — Berpindah Region itu rumit, berisiko melanggar residensi data, dan tidak menyelesaikan pola retry yang salah."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'ThrottlingException' → exponential backoff + jitter (SDK retry mode standard/adaptive)."},{"id":"E3A-57","d":3,"ts":"3.2.3","t":"Athena federated query","q":"Analysts use Amazon Athena to query clickstream data in Amazon S3. They now need to join it with customer records stored in Amazon DynamoDB and with order data in an on-premises MySQL database reachable through the VPC, without copying the data into S3 first. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Use AWS Glue jobs to export DynamoDB and MySQL data to S3 every hour, then query all three in Athena.","Use Amazon Redshift federated query because it supports DynamoDB and any JDBC source.","Deploy the Athena DynamoDB and MySQL data source connectors (which run as AWS Lambda functions), register them as data sources, and use Athena federated query to join them with the S3 tables.","Create Athena views over the DynamoDB tables directly in the AWS Glue Data Catalog."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'join S3 data with DynamoDB and MySQL' dan 'without copying the data into S3 first'. Athena federated query memakai data source connector yang berjalan sebagai fungsi AWS Lambda untuk membaca sumber non-S3 seperti DynamoDB, database JDBC (MySQL, PostgreSQL, dan lainnya), dan CloudWatch Logs. Setelah connector didaftarkan sebagai data source (catalog), satu query SQL Athena bisa menggabungkan tabel S3, DynamoDB, dan MySQL. Ekspor per jam dengan Glue justru menyalin data dan menambah pipeline. Redshift federated query hanya mendukung RDS/Aurora PostgreSQL dan MySQL, bukan DynamoDB. View Athena tidak bisa langsung membaca DynamoDB tanpa connector. Aturan umum: Athena + sumber non-S3 → federated query dengan connector Lambda.","r":["Salah — Menyalin data ke S3, melanggar syarat, dan menambah pipeline.","Salah — Redshift federated query hanya untuk RDS/Aurora PostgreSQL dan MySQL, bukan DynamoDB.","Benar — Connector Athena berbasis Lambda memungkinkan join S3, DynamoDB, dan MySQL dalam satu query tanpa menyalin data.","Salah — View Athena tidak bisa membaca DynamoDB tanpa data source connector."],"k":"Tips ujian: Athena query DynamoDB/JDBC/CloudWatch tanpa salin ke S3 → Athena federated query (connector Lambda)."},{"id":"E1C-46","d":1,"ts":"1.4.1","t":"Lambda execution environment reuse","q":"An AWS Lambda function enriches records by querying an Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL database. Profiling shows that each invocation spends 300 ms opening a new database connection and creating new AWS SDK clients, while the actual query takes 20 ms. The function is invoked thousands of times per minute. Which code change will reduce runtime the MOST?","o":["Increase the function timeout from 30 seconds to 5 minutes.","Open the connection and create the SDK clients inside the handler, then close them at the end of every invocation.","Create the database connection and SDK clients outside the handler function so they are reused across warm invocations of the same execution environment.","Add a time.sleep call before each query to reduce load on the database."],"a":[2],"e":"Profiling menunjukkan waktu habis untuk 'opening a new database connection and creating new AWS SDK clients' di setiap invocation. Kode di luar handler dijalankan sekali saat inisialisasi execution environment, dan objek seperti koneksi dan client SDK tetap tersedia untuk invocation berikutnya (warm start), sehingga overhead 300 ms hanya terjadi pada cold start. Ini praktik terbaik resmi Lambda; untuk banyak koneksi, Amazon RDS Proxy dapat menambah pooling. Distractor terdekat adalah membuat dan menutup koneksi di setiap invocation: justru pola yang menyebabkan masalah saat ini. Menaikkan timeout tidak mengurangi durasi. Menambah sleep memperlambat fungsi. Aturan umum: inisialisasi client dan koneksi di luar handler untuk reuse antar invocation.","r":["Salah — Timeout lebih panjang tidak mempercepat eksekusi.","Salah — Ini justru pola saat ini yang menyebabkan overhead 300 ms per invocation.","Benar — Objek yang dibuat di luar handler dipakai ulang pada warm invocation sehingga overhead koneksi hilang.","Salah — Sleep hanya menambah durasi dan biaya."],"k":"Tips ujian: Lambda lambat karena init koneksi/client → pindahkan ke luar handler (reuse execution environment)."},{"id":"E2C-34","d":2,"ts":"2.4.5","t":"Splittable compression and file sizing","q":"A team processes 10 TB of daily log files with Apache Spark on Amazon EMR. The files are currently single large gzip-compressed CSV files of about 20 GB each, and the job is slow because only a few executors are busy while reading. Downstream jobs read only a few columns. Which change will MOST improve read parallelism and downstream query efficiency?","o":["Recompress the files with gzip at a higher compression level.","Keep CSV format but remove compression entirely.","Convert the data to Apache Parquet with Snappy compression, using files of roughly 128 MB to 1 GB.","Convert the data to a single large JSON file per day."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah 'only a few executors are busy while reading' pada file gzip besar dan downstream 'read only a few columns'. File gzip tidak splittable, sehingga satu file 20 GB hanya bisa dibaca oleh satu task, yang membatasi paralelisme. Parquet dengan kompresi Snappy splittable pada level row group, kolumnar sehingga hanya kolom yang diperlukan yang dibaca, dan ukuran file sekitar 128 MB sampai 1 GB menyeimbangkan paralelisme dan overhead file. Level kompresi gzip yang lebih tinggi tetap tidak splittable dan menambah CPU. CSV tanpa kompresi bisa di-split, tetapi ukuran data dan I/O membengkak serta tetap row-based. JSON tunggal per hari tidak memperbaiki pembacaan kolom. Aturan umum: hindari file besar yang tidak splittable (gzip); gunakan format kolumnar dengan codec splittable dan ukuran file optimal.","r":["Salah — gzip tetap tidak splittable sehingga paralelisme tetap rendah, dan CPU dekompresi bertambah.","Salah — CSV tanpa kompresi bisa di-split tetapi memperbesar I/O dan tetap membaca semua kolom.","Benar — Parquet + Snappy splittable dan kolumnar, sehingga paralelisme tinggi dan hanya kolom yang dibutuhkan yang dibaca.","Salah — JSON besar per hari tetap row-based dan tidak efisien untuk membaca sebagian kolom."],"k":"Tips ujian: gzip tidak splittable → file besar = paralelisme rendah; pilih Parquet/ORC + Snappy."},{"id":"E2B-33","d":2,"ts":"2.3.1","t":"Redshift auto-copy from S3","q":"Partner systems drop small batches of CSV files into an S3 prefix at irregular times throughout the day. A data engineer must load each new file into an Amazon Redshift table, load each file only once, and avoid building schedulers, Lambda functions, or tracking tables. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that invokes an AWS Lambda function to run COPY for each new object.","Schedule an AWS Glue job every 5 minutes that lists the prefix and loads files that are not in a tracking table.","Create an S3 event integration between the bucket and the Redshift data warehouse, and then create a COPY JOB (Amazon Redshift auto-copy from Amazon S3) on the prefix so that Redshift automatically loads new files and tracks which files were loaded.","Run a COPY command for the whole prefix every hour by using the Redshift query scheduler."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci: file tiba 'at irregular times', 'load each file only once' dan 'avoid building schedulers, Lambda functions, or tracking tables'. Redshift auto-copy memakai S3 event integration (bucket dan data warehouse di Region yang sama) lalu COPY JOB (COPY ... JOB CREATE) pada prefix S3; Redshift mendeteksi file baru dan otomatis menjalankan COPY saat file baru tiba; Redshift juga mencatat file yang sudah dimuat sehingga tidak dimuat dua kali. Ini memenuhi semua syarat tanpa komponen tambahan. EventBridge plus Lambda berfungsi, tetapi justru komponen yang ingin dihindari, dan Anda harus menangani retry dan duplikasi sendiri. Glue job dengan tracking table menambah job dan tabel kontrol. COPY per jam untuk seluruh prefix memuat ulang file lama sehingga terjadi duplikasi. Ingat: continuous file ingestion S3 → Redshift tanpa orkestrasi → auto-copy (COPY JOB).","r":["Salah — Lambda dan EventBridge adalah komponen kustom yang ingin dihindari, dan perlu logika anti-duplikasi.","Salah — Glue job terjadwal dan tracking table menambah overhead yang ingin dihindari.","Benar — S3 event integration + COPY JOB memuat file baru otomatis dan melacak file yang sudah dimuat untuk mencegah duplikasi.","Salah — COPY berulang atas seluruh prefix memuat ulang file lama dan menyebabkan duplikasi."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'automatically load new S3 files into Redshift' + 'no duplicates' → Redshift auto-copy (S3 event integration + COPY ... JOB CREATE)."},{"id":"E1B-69","d":1,"ts":"1.2.10","t":"Reliable LLM output in data pipelines","q":"A data pipeline sends product descriptions to a foundation model on Amazon Bedrock and asks it to return attributes as JSON. The responses are complete, but some contain extra prose, missing keys, or different key names, which breaks the downstream loading step. Which TWO actions will MOST improve the reliability of the pipeline? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Set a low temperature and include an explicit JSON schema and a few examples of the expected output in the prompt.","Increase the maximum output tokens to the highest value supported by the model.","Validate every response against the JSON schema in the pipeline, and route invalid responses to a retry step or a quarantine location for review.","Immediately fine-tune a custom model on millions of labeled examples.","Purchase Provisioned Throughput for the model."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Penentunya adalah respons yang 'complete' tetapi formatnya tidak konsisten (prosa tambahan, key hilang, atau nama key berbeda) sehingga merusak tahap loading. Temperatur rendah membuat output lebih deterministik, dan prompt dengan skema JSON eksplisit serta contoh (few-shot) mengarahkan model ke format yang konsisten. Karena output LLM tetap probabilistik, pipeline juga harus memvalidasi setiap respons terhadap skema dan mengalihkan yang tidak valid ke retry atau lokasi karantina, mirip pola dead-letter queue. Menaikkan max tokens tidak relevan karena respons tidak terpotong. Fine-tuning langsung dengan jutaan contoh adalah usaha besar sebelum mencoba prompt engineering. Provisioned Throughput mengatasi kapasitas, bukan format. Aturan umum: LLM dalam pipeline data → prompt terstruktur + temperatur rendah + validasi output + penanganan record gagal.","r":["Benar — Temperatur rendah dan skema serta contoh di prompt meningkatkan konsistensi format output.","Salah — Respons sudah lengkap; menaikkan max tokens tidak memperbaiki format.","Benar — Validasi skema dan routing record tidak valid melindungi tahap downstream.","Salah — Fine-tuning besar adalah langkah mahal yang belum diperlukan untuk masalah format.","Salah — Provisioned Throughput menambah kapasitas, bukan memperbaiki format output."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'LLM output format inconsistent in pipeline' → prompt with schema/examples + low temperature + validate & quarantine."},{"id":"E2B-10","d":2,"ts":"2.2.3","t":"Glue crawler schema change policy","q":"A financial company uses an AWS Glue crawler to keep a Data Catalog table in sync with an S3 dataset that downstream Amazon Athena reports depend on. A recent upstream change caused the crawler to change a column's data type, which broke several reports. The company now requires that schema changes be reviewed by a data engineer before the catalog is changed, while new partitions must still be added automatically. Which crawler configuration meets these requirements?","o":["Set the schema change policy to 'Update the table definition in the Data Catalog' and the deletion behavior to 'Delete tables and partitions from the Data Catalog'.","Set the schema change policy to 'Ignore the change and don't update the table in the Data Catalog' (UpdateBehavior LOG), enable 'Update all new and existing partitions with metadata from the table', and review the logged schema changes in Amazon CloudWatch Logs.","Delete the crawler and run MSCK REPAIR TABLE from Athena after every upstream change.","Set the recrawl policy to crawl all folders and run the crawler only once a month."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: 'schema changes be reviewed ... before the catalog is changed' tetapi 'new partitions must still be added automatically'. Glue crawler punya schema change policy: UpdateBehavior bisa LOG (abaikan perubahan dan jangan update tabel) dan DeleteBehavior bisa LOG atau DEPRECATE. Dengan 'Ignore the change and don't update the table', crawler hanya mencatat perubahan skema ke CloudWatch Logs untuk direview, sedangkan tabel dan partisi baru tetap dibuat; opsi 'Update all new and existing partitions with metadata from the table' (InheritFromTable) membuat partisi mewarisi skema tabel. 'Update the table definition' adalah perilaku default yang justru menyebabkan laporan rusak. MSCK REPAIR hanya menambah partisi Hive-style, tidak ada review skema, dan menghapus crawler menghilangkan otomatisasi. Crawl bulanan membuat partisi baru terlambat. Ingat: 'jangan ubah skema otomatis' → schema change policy LOG/ignore.","r":["Salah — 'Update the table definition' adalah perilaku default dan justru memperbarui tipe kolom secara otomatis, penyebab masalah awal; menghapus tabel/partisi juga tidak diminta.","Benar — Dengan UpdateBehavior LOG skema tabel tidak diubah (perubahan hanya dicatat di log), partisi baru tetap dibuat, dan partisi mewarisi skema tabel.","Salah — MSCK REPAIR tidak memberi mekanisme review skema dan harus dijalankan manual.","Salah — Crawl bulanan menunda pendaftaran partisi baru dan tetap bisa mengubah skema tanpa review."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'prevent crawler from changing schema' → schema change policy = Ignore/LOG; deletion = LOG/DEPRECATE."},{"id":"E1A-32","d":1,"ts":"1.1.5","t":"Amazon MWAA","q":"A data platform team already maintains more than 200 Apache Airflow DAGs written in Python on a self-managed cluster. The DAGs include complex dependencies, backfills, and sensors across AWS Glue, Amazon EMR, and Amazon Redshift. The team wants to move scheduling to AWS with minimal rework and without managing Airflow infrastructure. Which service should the team use?","o":["AWS Glue workflows","Amazon EventBridge rules with one rule per task","Amazon Managed Workflows for Apache Airflow (Amazon MWAA)","AWS Step Functions with one state machine per DAG rewritten in Amazon States Language"],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci: '200 Apache Airflow DAGs', 'minimal rework', dan 'without managing Airflow infrastructure'. Amazon MWAA menjalankan Apache Airflow secara managed, sehingga DAG yang ada bisa dipindahkan hampir apa adanya (dengan penyesuaian dependensi dan connection), termasuk backfill, sensor, dan operator untuk Glue, EMR, dan Redshift. Distraktor terdekat adalah Step Functions: sangat baik untuk workflow serverless, tetapi semua DAG harus ditulis ulang dalam Amazon States Language. Glue workflows terbatas pada crawler dan job Glue. EventBridge rules tidak bisa mengelola dependensi antar-task yang kompleks. Aturan umum: sudah memakai Airflow atau butuh orkestrasi berbasis Python open source = MWAA.","r":["Salah — Glue workflows hanya mengorkestrasi job dan crawler Glue, dan DAG harus dibangun ulang.","Salah — EventBridge rules tidak bisa mengelola dependensi, sensor, dan backfill antar-task.","Benar — MWAA menjalankan Airflow secara managed sehingga DAG yang ada bisa dipakai dengan rework minimal.","Salah — Menulis ulang 200 DAG ke Amazon States Language adalah rework yang besar."],"k":"Sudah punya DAG Airflow → Amazon MWAA."},{"id":"E4A-46","d":4,"ts":"4.2.4","t":"Lake Formation cell-level security","q":"A healthcare company shares a patient visits table, governed by AWS Lake Formation, with an external research partner's analysts who use Amazon Athena. The analysts must see only visits where consent_research = true, and they must not see the patient_name, phone, and address columns; all other columns may be shown. All other users keep full access. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Create an Athena view that excludes the PII columns and grant the partner access to the S3 location of the table.","Grant the partner SELECT on only the non-PII columns, and ask the partner to add WHERE consent_research = true to its queries.","Use Amazon Macie to detect PII in the table and automatically block access for the partner.","Create a Lake Formation data filter with the row filter expression consent_research = true and a column list that includes only the non-PII columns (omitting patient_name, phone, and address), and grant SELECT on the table through this data filter."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci: kombinasi 'only visits where consent_research = true' (baris) dan 'must not see ... columns' (kolom). Lake Formation data filter dapat menggabungkan row filter expression dengan daftar kolom; kombinasi ini disebut cell-level security. Untuk berbagi lintas akun yang di-query lewat Athena, gunakan daftar kolom inclusion (hanya kolom yang boleh dilihat), karena Athena dan Redshift Spectrum hanya mendukung column-level access control berbasis inclusion untuk resource yang dibagikan lintas akun. Grant SELECT melalui data filter memastikan pembatasan baris dan kolom ditegakkan bersama oleh Lake Formation tanpa memengaruhi user lain. Grant pada kolom non-PII saja memenuhi pembatasan kolom, tetapi filter baris yang bergantung pada kepatuhan partner tidak bisa ditegakkan. Akses ke lokasi S3 melewati view dan mengekspos seluruh data. Macie mendeteksi PII tetapi tidak menegakkan izin akses per baris dan kolom. Aturan umum: baris + kolom sekaligus → data filter cell-level di Lake Formation.","r":["Salah — Akses ke lokasi S3 memberi data mentah lengkap sehingga view tidak berarti.","Salah — Pembatasan kolom ditegakkan, tetapi filter baris bergantung pada partner dan bisa dihindari.","Salah — Macie menemukan data sensitif, bukan menegakkan izin akses per baris dan kolom.","Benar — Data filter dengan row filter dan daftar kolom yang diizinkan menegakkan cell-level security."],"k":"Tips ujian: row filter + pembatasan kolom dalam satu grant → Lake Formation data filter (cell-level security); lintas akun via Athena → pakai column inclusion."},{"id":"E2A-45","d":2,"ts":"2.1.5","t":"Redshift hot/cold data with Spectrum","q":"A Redshift cluster stores 5 years of transaction data, but 95% of queries access only the most recent 6 months. Storage costs are growing and the company wants to reduce them without losing the ability to run occasional SQL queries over all 5 years from Redshift. What should a data engineer do?","o":["Delete data older than 6 months from Redshift and restore it from snapshots when needed.","Keep all data in Redshift and enable automatic table compression on every table.","Copy the older data to Amazon DynamoDB and query it with PartiQL.","Unload data older than 6 months to Amazon S3 in partitioned Parquet format, delete it from the Redshift tables, and query it through Redshift Spectrum when needed."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci adalah '95% of queries access only the most recent 6 months', ingin 'reduce' biaya storage, dan tetap bisa 'run occasional SQL queries over all 5 years from Redshift'. Pola hot/cold yang direkomendasikan adalah menyimpan data panas di tabel Redshift lokal dan memindahkan data dingin dengan UNLOAD ke S3 dalam format kolumnar terpartisi, lalu mengaksesnya melalui Redshift Spectrum; dengan view gabungan (late-binding view) analis bisa melihat seluruh rentang. S3 jauh lebih murah dibanding storage cluster, dan Spectrum hanya ditagih per data yang dipindai. Distraktor terdekat adalah kompresi otomatis: menghemat ruang tetapi tidak cukup untuk data yang terus tumbuh. Restore dari snapshot lambat dan tidak praktis untuk query sesekali. DynamoDB tidak cocok untuk query analitik SQL. Aturan umum: data dingin warehouse → S3 Parquet + Spectrum; data panas → tabel lokal Redshift.","r":["Salah — Restore snapshot untuk setiap query historis lambat, mahal, dan merepotkan.","Salah — Kompresi hanya mengurangi sebagian storage dan data dingin tetap memakan kapasitas cluster.","Salah — DynamoDB tidak dirancang untuk query analitik skala besar dan tidak terintegrasi dengan query Redshift.","Benar — Data dingin di S3 Parquet murah dan tetap dapat di-query dari Redshift melalui Spectrum bersama data panas."],"k":"Hot data in Redshift, cold data in S3 Parquet via Spectrum → lower cost, still queryable."},{"id":"E4B-23","d":4,"ts":"4.4.1","t":"CloudTrail event history","q":"A data engineer discovers that an AWS Glue Data Catalog table used by a production pipeline was deleted yesterday. The engineer needs to identify which IAM principal performed the deletion and from which IP address. The company has not configured any trails. What is the FASTEST way to find this information?","o":["Search the AWS CloudTrail event history for the DeleteTable event from the AWS Glue event source.","Review the AWS Config configuration timeline of the IAM role that the pipeline uses.","Query the Amazon CloudWatch metrics for AWS Glue to find the time of the deletion.","Search the CloudWatch Logs log group of the Glue job for the deletion message."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: identifikasi 'which IAM principal' dan 'from which IP address' untuk kejadian 'yesterday', dan 'has not configured any trails'. CloudTrail event history selalu aktif tanpa konfigurasi dan menyimpan management events (seperti glue:DeleteTable) selama 90 hari, termasuk userIdentity, sourceIPAddress, dan waktu kejadian. Karena DeleteTable adalah management event, informasinya tersedia langsung. Distraktor terdekat adalah AWS Config timeline untuk IAM role: Config merekam perubahan konfigurasi role itu sendiri, bukan siapa yang memanggil API penghapusan tabel. CloudWatch metrics tidak menyimpan identitas pemanggil. Log job Glue berisi output aplikasi job, bukan panggilan API dari principal lain. Aturan umum: 'who did what, when, from where' pada API AWS → CloudTrail (event history 90 hari untuk management events).","r":["Benar — Event history CloudTrail menyimpan management events 90 hari, termasuk identitas dan IP pemanggil, tanpa trail.","Salah — Config merekam konfigurasi resource IAM role, bukan siapa yang memanggil DeleteTable.","Salah — Metrics hanya berisi angka agregat tanpa identitas pemanggil.","Salah — Log job berisi output aplikasi, bukan catatan panggilan API oleh principal lain."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'who deleted/changed, last 90 days, no trail' → CloudTrail event history."},{"id":"E1C-10","d":1,"ts":"1.3.1","t":"Step Functions nested workflows","q":"A company has 12 AWS Step Functions Standard workflows, one for each data domain. Every workflow ends with the same sequence of steps: run validation queries, update the AWS Glue Data Catalog table description, and publish a completion event. The sequence is copied into every state machine, so each change must be made 12 times. Each parent workflow must wait for the shared steps to finish, use their output, and fail if they fail. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Move the shared steps into one AWS Lambda function that each workflow invokes and that runs the steps in sequence with AWS SDK calls.","Have each parent workflow publish a message to an Amazon SNS topic that starts the shared steps, and continue to the end of the workflow immediately.","Create one shared Standard state machine for the common steps and call it from each parent workflow with a Step Functions StartExecution task that uses the .sync:2 integration pattern.","Use a Parallel state in each workflow so that the copied steps run faster."],"a":[2],"e":"Kebutuhannya: langkah yang sama 'copied into every state machine' sehingga perubahan dilakukan 12 kali, dan parent workflow harus 'wait for the shared steps to finish, use their output, and fail if they fail'. Step Functions mendukung nested workflow: satu state machine dapat memulai state machine lain lewat integrasi StartExecution. Dengan pola '.sync' (varian '.sync:2' mengembalikan output child sebagai JSON), parent menunggu child selesai, menerima output-nya, dan task gagal jika eksekusi child gagal. Logika bersama cukup dipelihara di satu state machine, dan eksekusi child tetap terlihat di konsol. Distractor terdekat adalah memindahkan semuanya ke satu Lambda: duplikasi hilang, tetapi Anda menulis kode orkestrasi sendiri, kehilangan visibilitas per step, dan terikat timeout 15 menit. SNS bersifat fire-and-forget sehingga parent tidak menunggu dan tidak gagal bila langkah bersama gagal. Parallel state tidak menghapus duplikasi. Aturan umum: pakai ulang sub-proses antar workflow → nested state machine dengan StartExecution .sync.","r":["Salah — Menghapus duplikasi, tetapi menjadi kode orkestrasi kustom tanpa visibilitas per step dan dibatasi timeout 15 menit.","Salah — Publish ke SNS tidak menunggu hasil, sehingga parent tidak bisa memakai output atau gagal saat langkah bersama gagal.","Benar — Child state machine bersama dipanggil dengan StartExecution .sync:2, sehingga parent menunggu, menerima output, dan gagal bila child gagal.","Salah — Langkah tetap disalin di setiap workflow; Parallel hanya menjalankan cabang secara bersamaan."],"k":"Tips ujian: logika workflow yang dipakai ulang + parent harus menunggu → nested state machine (StartExecution .sync / .sync:2)."},{"id":"E4B-58","d":4,"ts":"4.5.6","t":"SageMaker Catalog unmanaged asset grants","q":"A company publishes a custom asset type in Amazon SageMaker Catalog that represents data in a third-party system. This type is an unmanaged asset, so SageMaker Catalog does not grant access automatically. The company wants consumers to receive access automatically as soon as a data owner approves their subscription request, without polling. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Ask data owners to email the platform team after each approval so that the team can grant access manually.","Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that matches the SageMaker Catalog subscription approval event and invokes an AWS Lambda function that grants access in the third-party system.","Run a scheduled AWS Glue job every hour that lists all subscriptions and grants access for new approvals.","Convert the asset to an AWS Glue table by copying the data into Amazon S3 every night."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: 'unmanaged asset' yang tidak di-grant otomatis, akses harus diberikan 'as soon as a data owner approves', 'without polling', dan 'LEAST operational overhead'. Untuk unmanaged asset, SageMaker Catalog (Amazon DataZone) tetap memancarkan event ke Amazon EventBridge saat subscription disetujui, sehingga Anda dapat membuat custom grant handler: rule EventBridge memicu Lambda yang memberikan izin di sistem target. Pendekatan event-driven ini segera dan serverless. Distraktor terdekat adalah Glue job terjadwal: berfungsi, tetapi berbasis polling, terlambat hingga satu jam, dan menambah resource. Proses email manual lambat dan rawan kesalahan. Menyalin data ke S3 setiap malam mengubah arsitektur, menduplikasi data, dan membuat data basi. Aturan umum: unmanaged asset di SageMaker Catalog → EventBridge event + Lambda sebagai custom grant handler.","r":["Salah — Proses manual lambat, tidak otomatis, dan rawan kesalahan.","Benar — Event approval di EventBridge memicu Lambda untuk memberi akses segera tanpa polling.","Salah — Job terjadwal adalah polling, terlambat, dan menambah resource untuk dikelola.","Salah — Menyalin data menciptakan duplikasi dan data basi hanya untuk menghindari grant kustom."],"k":"Tips ujian: SageMaker Catalog unmanaged asset → subscription events in EventBridge → Lambda custom grant."},{"id":"E1B-10","d":1,"ts":"1.2.5","t":"Glue streaming ETL vs Firehose vs Flink","q":"A company streams IoT sensor readings into Amazon Kinesis Data Streams. Every few minutes, a data engineer must deduplicate the readings, join them with device reference data stored as Parquet in Amazon S3, and write partitioned Parquet output to the data lake. A latency of a few minutes is acceptable. The team has strong PySpark skills but no Java or Flink experience. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Use Amazon Data Firehose with record format conversion to write Parquet directly to Amazon S3.","Run Spark Structured Streaming on a long-running Amazon EMR cluster on Amazon EC2.","Create an AWS Glue streaming ETL job in PySpark that reads from Kinesis, joins with the reference data, and writes partitioned Parquet.","Build a Java application on Amazon Managed Service for Apache Flink that performs the join and deduplication."],"a":[2],"e":"Kebutuhan penentunya adalah deduplikasi dan join dengan data referensi di S3, latensi 'a few minutes' yang dapat diterima, skill 'PySpark' tanpa pengalaman Flink, dan 'LEAST operational overhead'. AWS Glue streaming ETL job menjalankan Spark Structured Streaming secara serverless dalam micro-batch, dapat membaca Kinesis, melakukan join dengan data S3, dan menulis Parquet terpartisi. Firehose dengan format conversion adalah distraktor terdekat karena paling sederhana, tetapi Firehose tidak bisa melakukan join dengan data referensi atau deduplikasi. EMR on EC2 membutuhkan pengelolaan cluster yang terus berjalan. Flink dengan Java tidak sesuai dengan skill tim. Aturan umum: streaming dengan latensi menit, logika Spark, dan serverless → Glue streaming ETL.","r":["Salah — Firehose hanya mengonversi format dan mengirim data; tidak mendukung join dengan data referensi maupun deduplikasi.","Salah — Cluster EMR yang berjalan terus menambah beban pengelolaan dan biaya.","Benar — Glue streaming ETL adalah Spark Structured Streaming serverless yang sesuai skill PySpark dan kebutuhan join/dedup.","Salah — Membutuhkan Java dan Flink, yang tidak dikuasai tim."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'streaming + PySpark + minute-level latency + serverless' → Glue streaming ETL; 'sub-second + complex state' → Flink."},{"id":"E3A-69","d":3,"ts":"3.2.6","t":"Window functions vs GROUP BY","q":"A report must show every individual order row with its order_id, customer_id, and amount, plus a column showing that customer's total spend across all orders and the order's percentage of that total. A data engineer first tried GROUP BY customer_id, but the individual order rows disappeared. Which SQL approach meets the requirement in Amazon Redshift or Amazon Athena?","o":["Use GROUP BY customer_id, order_id, amount and SUM(amount).","Use SELECT DISTINCT customer_id, SUM(amount) without GROUP BY.","Use a window function: SUM(amount) OVER (PARTITION BY customer_id) AS customer_total, and divide amount by customer_total for the percentage.","Use GROUP BY ROLLUP (customer_id) to add a subtotal row for each customer."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'show every individual order row' plus 'customer's total' di setiap baris. GROUP BY merangkum banyak baris menjadi satu baris per grup, sehingga detail order hilang. Window function dengan SUM(amount) OVER (PARTITION BY customer_id) menghitung total per customer tetapi mempertahankan setiap baris asli, sehingga total dan persentase (amount / customer_total) bisa ditampilkan di samping setiap order. GROUP BY customer_id, order_id, amount hanya menjumlahkan setiap order dengan dirinya sendiri, bukan total customer. SELECT DISTINCT dengan SUM tanpa GROUP BY tidak valid jika customer_id tidak diagregasi. ROLLUP menambahkan baris subtotal terpisah, bukan kolom total di setiap baris order. Aturan umum: butuh agregat sambil mempertahankan detail baris → window function (OVER PARTITION BY); butuh ringkasan per grup → GROUP BY.","r":["Salah — Setiap grup berisi satu order, sehingga SUM sama dengan amount, bukan total customer.","Salah — SQL tidak valid karena customer_id tidak diagregasi tanpa GROUP BY.","Benar — Window SUM per customer mempertahankan setiap baris order dan menambahkan total serta persentase.","Salah — ROLLUP menambah baris subtotal terpisah, bukan kolom total di setiap baris."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'keep row-level detail + show group total' → window function SUM() OVER (PARTITION BY ...), bukan GROUP BY."},{"id":"E3B-18","d":3,"ts":"3.3.3","t":"SNS and SQS fan-out for alerts","q":"When a nightly pipeline fails, two consumers must be notified: the on-call engineers by email, and an internal ticketing service that pulls work over HTTPS and is sometimes offline for maintenance for up to 2 hours. No failure notification can be lost. Which TWO actions should a data engineer take? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Publish pipeline failure events to an Amazon SNS topic with an email subscription for the on-call engineers.","Subscribe an Amazon SQS queue to the SNS topic so the ticketing service can poll the queue when it is back online.","Send failure notifications to the ticketing service by using Amazon SES.","Write failure messages to a CloudWatch Logs log group and have the ticketing service run Logs Insights queries every 2 hours.","Configure the ticketing service to subscribe directly to the SNS topic through an HTTPS endpoint with no other buffering."],"a":[0,1],"e":"Persyaratannya: fan-out ke dua konsumen dan 'no failure notification can be lost' meskipun layanan tiket 'offline for up to 2 hours'. SNS topic memberi fan-out: email untuk engineer dan SQS queue sebagai subscriber. SQS menyimpan pesan secara tahan lama (retensi default 4 hari, bisa hingga 14 hari) sehingga layanan tiket dapat menarik pesan setelah online lagi. Distraktor terdekat adalah langganan HTTPS langsung ke SNS: SNS memang melakukan retry, tetapi kebijakan retry HTTP terbatas sehingga downtime 2 jam berisiko kehilangan pesan tanpa buffer. SES di luar cakupan ujian dan tidak cocok untuk integrasi sistem. Polling Logs Insights rapuh dan bukan mekanisme notifikasi. Aturan: SNS untuk fan-out, SQS untuk buffering konsumen yang bisa offline.","r":["Benar — SNS topic mengirim notifikasi email ke engineer dan menjadi titik fan-out.","Benar — SQS queue yang disubscribe ke SNS menyimpan pesan dengan aman sampai layanan tiket kembali online.","Salah — SES adalah layanan email (di luar cakupan) dan tidak menyediakan antrean tahan lama untuk sistem tiket.","Salah — Query log berkala bukan mekanisme pengiriman notifikasi dan mudah melewatkan event.","Salah — Retry HTTPS SNS terbatas, sehingga downtime 2 jam dapat menyebabkan notifikasi hilang."],"k":"Tips ujian: konsumen yang bisa down/harus pull → SNS + SQS fan-out (jangan langsung HTTPS)."},{"id":"E3A-44","d":3,"ts":"3.2.4","t":"Athena Spark-enabled workgroups","q":"A data engineer opens the Amazon Athena console in the default 'primary' workgroup and wants to create a notebook to run PySpark code. The notebook option is not available, although SQL queries run normally. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Create a new Athena workgroup that uses the Apache Spark analytics engine (PySpark engine version 3) with an IAM role for the sessions, and then create the notebook in that workgroup.","Upgrade the primary workgroup to Athena SQL engine version 3.","Enable query result reuse in the primary workgroup.","Install Apache Spark on an Amazon EC2 instance and register it as an Athena data source connector."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'primary workgroup' dan 'notebook option is not available'. Di Athena, setiap workgroup memiliki satu jenis analytics engine: Athena SQL atau Apache Spark. Notebook PySpark hanya tersedia di workgroup yang dibuat dengan engine Apache Spark, dan workgroup itu memerlukan IAM role yang dipakai session untuk mengakses S3 dan Glue Data Catalog. Workgroup 'primary' adalah workgroup SQL, jadi solusinya membuat workgroup Spark baru. Athena SQL engine version 3 adalah versi engine SQL (berbasis Trino), berbeda dengan PySpark engine version 3, dan tidak menambah notebook. Query result reuse adalah fitur SQL untuk menghemat biaya. Data source connector berbasis Lambda dipakai untuk federated query, bukan untuk menjalankan Spark. Aturan umum: Athena notebook Spark → workgroup dengan engine Apache Spark (terpisah dari workgroup SQL).","r":["Benar — Notebook hanya tersedia di workgroup dengan engine Apache Spark yang dilengkapi IAM role untuk session.","Salah — Athena SQL engine version 3 tetap engine SQL dan tidak menyediakan notebook Spark.","Salah — Result reuse hanya fitur penghematan untuk query SQL.","Salah — Connector federated query tidak menjalankan Spark atau notebook."],"k":"Tips ujian: notebook Spark di Athena butuh workgroup engine 'Apache Spark', bukan workgroup SQL."},{"id":"E1A-68","d":1,"ts":"1.1.12","t":"Stateful stream processing with Flink","q":"A streaming application must compute, for each user, the number of transactions in 5-minute sliding windows and detect when a user exceeds a threshold. The results must be accurate even if the application restarts, with exactly-once state consistency and sub-second latency. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["An AWS Lambda function triggered by Kinesis Data Streams that keeps counts in global variables.","Amazon Data Firehose with a Lambda transformation that counts records per user.","Amazon Managed Service for Apache Flink reading from Kinesis Data Streams, using keyed state and windows with checkpointing enabled.","An AWS Glue batch job that runs every 5 minutes and counts transactions per user."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci: hitungan per user dalam '5-minute sliding windows', 'accurate even if the application restarts', 'exactly-once state consistency', dan 'sub-second latency'. Ini adalah pemrosesan stateful: aplikasi harus mengingat jumlah transaksi per user lintas banyak record. Amazon Managed Service for Apache Flink menyediakan keyed state, berbagai tipe window (termasuk sliding), serta checkpoint dan snapshot terkelola yang memberi konsistensi state exactly-once dan pemulihan setelah restart. Distraktor terdekat adalah Lambda dengan variabel global: Lambda bersifat stateless; variabel global hilang saat execution environment berganti dan tidak dibagi antar-invocation paralel. Firehose transformation bersifat per-record (stateless). Glue batch tiap 5 menit tidak sub-detik dan tidak memberi sliding window yang kontinu. Aturan umum: agregasi window, deduplikasi, atau join streaming dengan state tahan restart = Flink.","r":["Salah — Variabel global Lambda tidak tahan restart dan tidak dibagi antar-invocation, sehingga hitungan tidak akurat.","Salah — Transformasi Firehose bersifat per-record dan tidak menyimpan state lintas record.","Benar — Flink menyediakan keyed state, sliding windows, dan checkpointing untuk konsistensi exactly-once.","Salah — Batch tiap 5 menit tidak memenuhi latensi sub-detik dan bukan sliding window kontinu."],"k":"Stateful streaming (window, per-key state, exactly-once, tahan restart) → Managed Service for Apache Flink."},{"id":"E4A-12","d":4,"ts":"4.1.3","t":"Caching rotated secrets in Lambda","q":"An AWS Lambda function loads data into an Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL database. The function reads the database password from AWS Secrets Manager once during initialization and keeps it in memory. After Secrets Manager rotates the password, warm Lambda execution environments fail with authentication errors until they are recycled. The company wants to keep rotation enabled and minimize calls to Secrets Manager. Which TWO changes should a data engineer make? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Store the password in a Lambda environment variable and update the variable after each rotation.","Disable automatic rotation and rotate the password manually during maintenance windows.","Use the AWS Parameters and Secrets Lambda Extension to cache the secret with a time-to-live that is much shorter than the rotation interval.","Configure the function to always read the AWSPREVIOUS staging label of the secret.","On an authentication failure, have the function fetch the AWSCURRENT version of the secret again and retry the connection."],"a":[2,4],"e":"Kata kunci: 'keep rotation enabled' dan 'minimize calls to Secrets Manager'. Akar masalahnya adalah cache yang tidak pernah kedaluwarsa. AWS Parameters and Secrets Lambda Extension menyediakan cache lokal dengan TTL, sehingga panggilan API berkurang tetapi nilai tetap diperbarui secara berkala. Pola kedua adalah 'retry on auth failure': jika login gagal, ambil ulang AWSCURRENT lalu coba lagi, sehingga jeda singkat setelah rotasi tertangani. Environment variable menyimpan password dalam konfigurasi dan perlu update manual setelah setiap rotasi. Menonaktifkan rotasi melanggar kebutuhan. AWSPREVIOUS adalah password lama yang tidak valid lagi. Aturan umum: cache secret dengan TTL + refresh saat gagal autentikasi.","r":["Salah — Environment variable butuh update manual setiap rotasi dan mengekspos secret di konfigurasi fungsi.","Salah — Melanggar kebutuhan agar rotasi tetap aktif.","Benar — Extension menyediakan cache ber-TTL sehingga jumlah panggilan API berkurang dan nilai tetap diperbarui.","Salah — AWSPREVIOUS adalah versi lama yang tidak lagi berlaku setelah rotasi.","Benar — Mengambil ulang AWSCURRENT saat gagal login menangani perubahan password tanpa menunggu environment didaur ulang."],"k":"Tips ujian: Lambda + secret rotasi → Parameters and Secrets Lambda Extension (cache TTL) + refetch saat auth error."},{"id":"E3A-23","d":3,"ts":"3.1.6","t":"DataBrew PII masking","q":"A data team must prepare a customer dataset that contains email addresses and phone numbers before sharing it with an analytics team. The analytics team needs to join on these columns, so the values must be replaced consistently with irreversible tokens rather than removed. The data stewards want a visual tool and no custom code. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Use AWS Glue DataBrew to detect the PII columns and apply a cryptographic hash transformation that uses a secret stored in AWS Secrets Manager.","Use AWS Glue DataBrew to delete the email and phone columns before sharing.","Use Amazon Macie to scan the dataset and automatically replace the values in place.","Use an AWS Lambda function with custom code to encrypt the columns with an AWS KMS key."],"a":[0],"e":"Persyaratannya: nilai harus diganti 'consistently with irreversible tokens' agar tetap bisa di-join, memakai 'visual tool and no custom code'. DataBrew punya fitur deteksi PII dan transformasi masking, termasuk cryptographic hash yang memakai secret dari AWS Secrets Manager. Nilai yang sama selalu menghasilkan hash yang sama sehingga join tetap berfungsi, sementara nilai asli tidak bisa dikembalikan. Menghapus kolom melanggar kebutuhan join. Macie menemukan dan melaporkan data sensitif di S3, tetapi tidak mengubah isi data. Enkripsi KMS lewat Lambda membutuhkan kode dan sifatnya bisa didekripsi (reversible), bukan token yang tidak bisa dibalik. Aturan umum: masking PII secara visual saat persiapan data → DataBrew PII transformations.","r":["Benar — Hash kriptografis di DataBrew menghasilkan token konsisten yang tidak bisa dibalik, tanpa kode.","Salah — Menghapus kolom membuat analis tidak bisa melakukan join.","Salah — Macie hanya menemukan dan melaporkan data sensitif, tidak mengganti nilainya.","Salah — Membutuhkan kode kustom dan hasil enkripsi bisa didekripsi, jadi tidak irreversible."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'mask PII but keep joinable, no code' → DataBrew cryptographic hash (secret di Secrets Manager)."},{"id":"E3B-69","d":3,"ts":"3.4.5","t":"Detecting skew with Glue observability metrics","q":"A data engineer runs AWS Glue 4.0 Spark jobs and suspects that some runs are slow because of data skew, but the team has no visibility into skew without manually inspecting each run. The engineer wants a metric that quantifies skew per run and can be used in a CloudWatch alarm. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Enable CloudTrail data events for AWS Glue and count the events per job run.","Enable AWS Glue job observability metrics and create a CloudWatch alarm on the glue.driver.skewness.job metric.","Enable continuous logging and search the logs for the word 'skew'.","Enable job bookmarks to record the amount of data processed per run."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'a metric that quantifies skew per run' yang dapat dipakai untuk 'CloudWatch alarm' di 'AWS Glue 4.0'. AWS Glue job observability metrics (diaktifkan dengan --enable-observability-metrics, Glue 4.0 ke atas) menerbitkan metrik seperti glue.driver.skewness.stage dan glue.driver.skewness.job yang membandingkan durasi task terlama dengan median untuk mendeteksi skew data input maupun join yang skewed. Metrik ini ada di CloudWatch sehingga dapat diberi alarm. Distraktor terdekat adalah mencari kata 'skew' di log: Spark tidak menulis pesan seperti itu secara otomatis, sehingga tidak memberi ukuran kuantitatif. CloudTrail dan bookmarks tidak berhubungan dengan distribusi task. Aturan: deteksi skew di Glue → observability metrics (skewness) + Spark UI; perbaiki dengan salting/broadcast/repartition.","r":["Salah — CloudTrail mencatat panggilan API, bukan distribusi beban antar task.","Benar — Observability metrics menerbitkan metrik skewness per stage dan per job yang bisa diberi alarm CloudWatch.","Salah — Spark tidak secara otomatis menulis pesan 'skew', jadi pencarian log tidak mengukur skew.","Salah — Bookmarks melacak data yang sudah diproses, bukan ketimpangan beban task."],"k":"Tips ujian: Glue skew visibility → job observability metrics (glue.driver.skewness.stage/job)."},{"id":"E4A-23","d":4,"ts":"4.1.6","t":"Managed RDS IAM authentication vs self-managed DB","q":"A team runs PostgreSQL on self-managed Amazon EC2 instances. Applications authenticate with database passwords that are stored in configuration files. The security team wants applications to authenticate by using their IAM roles and short-lived tokens instead of database passwords, with the LEAST operational overhead. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Install a custom PAM module on the EC2 instances that validates IAM credentials on each login.","Store the passwords in AWS Secrets Manager and rotate them daily on the EC2 instances.","Configure the EC2 instance profile role so that PostgreSQL automatically trusts it.","Migrate the database to Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL and enable IAM database authentication, granting the application roles rds-db:connect for the database user."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci: 'authenticate by using their IAM roles and short-lived tokens' dan 'LEAST operational overhead'. Database yang di-host sendiri di EC2 adalah unmanaged service sehingga tidak terintegrasi otomatis dengan IAM. Amazon RDS dan Aurora (managed) mendukung IAM database authentication: aplikasi memanggil generate-db-auth-token dengan role-nya dan mendapat token yang berlaku 15 menit, dan IAM policy rds-db:connect mengatur user database mana yang boleh dipakai. Modul PAM custom bisa dibuat, tetapi menambah overhead pemeliharaan besar. Secrets Manager memperbaiki penyimpanan password, tetapi tetap memakai password, bukan identitas IAM. PostgreSQL di EC2 tidak bisa 'mempercayai' instance profile secara bawaan. Aturan umum: integrasi native dengan IAM adalah salah satu keuntungan memilih managed service dibanding unmanaged.","r":["Salah — Solusi custom seperti ini membutuhkan pengembangan dan pemeliharaan yang besar.","Salah — Masih memakai password, bukan autentikasi berbasis IAM role dan token.","Salah — PostgreSQL self-managed tidak punya integrasi bawaan dengan instance profile IAM.","Benar — RDS mendukung IAM database authentication dengan token sementara, dan izin diatur lewat rds-db:connect."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'authenticate to DB with IAM, no passwords' → RDS/Aurora IAM database authentication (token 15 menit, rds-db:connect)."}]});